return {
  ["creature.sir-braford.tftyp2014"]={title="Sir Braford",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 19 (3d8 + 6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 9 | CON 14 | INT 10 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBarkskin\n\nSir Braford's AC can't be lower than 16.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nSir Braford wields TftYP, a magic longsword that grants a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with it (included in his attack). See the Shatterspike handout for the item's other properties.\n\nTree Thrall\n\nIf the Gulthias Tree dies, Sir Braford dies 24 hours later.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage, or 9 (1d10 + 4) slashing damage if used with two hands.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nProtection\n\nWhen a creature Sir Braford can see attacks a target other than him that is within 5 feet of him, he can use a reaction to use his shield to impose disadvantage on the attack roll."},
  ["creature.sir-godfrey-gwilym.cos2014"]={title="Sir Godfrey Gwilym",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 139\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nCR: 6\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting"},
  ["creature.sir-jared.bmt2014"]={title="Sir Jared",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 80\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 17 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Halfling\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nJared makes three Longsword attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) slashing damage plus 4 (1d8) radiant damage. On a roll of 19 or 20, Jared scores a critical hit.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nProtect Ally\n\nWhen a creature Jared can see attacks a target other than Jared that is within 5 feet of him, Jared imposes disadvantage on the attack roll."},
  ["creature.sir-talavar.wbtw2014"]={title="Sir Talavar",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 69\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / T\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 14 (4d4 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 3 | DEX 20 | CON 13 | INT 14 | WIS 12 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSuperior Invisibility\n\nAs a bonus action, Sir Talavar can magically turn invisible until his concentration ends (as if concentration on a spell). Any equipment Sir Talavar wears or carries is invisible with him.\n\nLimited Telepathy\n\nUsing telepathy, Sir Talavar can magically communicate with any other faerie dragon within 60 feet of him.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSir Talavar has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\n+1 Tiny Sword\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d4 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nBite\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h1 piercing damage.\n\nEuphoria Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nSir Talavar exhales a puff of euphoria gas at one creature within 5 feet of him. The target must succeed on a 11 Wisdom saving throw, or for 1 minute, the target can't take reactions and must roll a d6 at the start of each of its turns to determine its behavior during the turn:\n\n• 1-4 The target takes no action or bonus action and uses all of its movement to move in a random direction.\n\n• 5-6 The target doesn't move, and the only thing it can do on its turn is make a 11 Wisdom saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.sir-ursas.imr2014"]={title="Sir Ursas",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 56\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 10 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Infernal\n\nResistencias: fire\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nSir Ursas wears a ring of mind shielding and plate armor of fire resistance.\n\nBrave\n\nSir Ursas has advantage on saving throws against being frightened.\n\nBrute\n\nA melee weapon deals one extra die of its damage when Sir Ursas hits with it (included in his attack).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSir Ursas makes three melee attacks or two ranged attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nSpear\n\nmw,rw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft. and range 20/60 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) piercing damage, or 13 (2d8 + 4) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack.\n\nShield Bash\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (2d4 + 4) bludgeoning damage, and if the target is a Medium or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 15 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nSir Ursas adds 3 to his AC against one melee attack that would hit him. To do so, he must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.sirac-of-suzail.skt2014"]={title="Sirac of Suzail",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 247\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 22 (5d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 17 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 13 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Orc\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nRoleplaying Information\n\nAn acolyte of Torm, Sirac grew up on the streets of Suzail, the capital of Cormyr. He came to Icewind Dale to become a knucklehead trout fisher but instead found religion. The misbegotten son of Artus Cimber, a renowned human adventurer, Sirac hasn't seen his father since he was a baby.\n\nIdeal: \"Without duty or loyalty, a man is nothing.\"\n\nBond: \"Icewind Dale is where i belong for the rest of my life.\"\n\nFlaw: \"I am honest to a fault.\"\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage.\n\nDart\n\nrw 5 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) piercing damage. Sirac carries six darts.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nParry\n\nSirac adds 2 to his AC against on melee attack that would hit him. To do so, Sirac must see the attacker and be wielding a melee weapon."},
  ["creature.sire-of-insanity.ggr2014"]={title="Sire of Insanity",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 197\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / H\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 157 (15d12 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 6 | CON 19 | INT 14 | WIS 19 | CHA 22\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: cold, fire, lightning\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Mind Erosion\n\nAny creature that starts its turn within 30 feet of the sire must make a 18 Wisdom saving throw. On a successful save, the creature is immune to this aura for the next 24 hours. On a failed save, the creature has disadvantage for 1 minute on Wisdom and Charisma checks and on Wisdom and Charisma saves. At the start of each of its turns, the sire can suppress this aura until the start of its next turn.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe sire has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sire makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h25 (3d12 + 6) piercing damage plus 16 (3d10) psychic damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h10 (1d8 + 6) slashing damage plus 9 (2d8) psychic damage."},
  ["language.siren.psx2014"]={title="Siren",subtitle="Idioma - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 17"},
  ["species.siren.psx2014"]={title="Siren",subtitle="Especie - PSX - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nAlignment\n\nMost sirens lean toward chaotic alignment, cherishing the freedom and independence that comes from joining a pirate crew.\n\nSize\n\nSirens stand about 5 to 6 feet tall, but their bodies are slender and their bones partially hollow to facilitate their flight. Your size is Medium.\n\nSiren's Song\n\nYou know the friends cantrip and can cast it without material components.\n\nFlight\n\nYou have a flying speed of 30 feet. You can't use your flying speed while you wear medium or heavy armor. (If your campaign uses the variant rule for PHB, you can't use your flying speed if you are encumbered.)\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can speak, read, and write PSX (if it exists in your campaign) and PSX."},
  ["creature.siren.tftyp2014"]={title="Siren",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 243\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 38 (7d8 + 7)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 18 | CON 12 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nSiren can breathe air and water.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSiren has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nStupefying Touch\n\nSiren touches one creature she can see within 5 feet of her. The creature must succeed on a 13 Intelligence saving throw or take 13 (3d6 + 3) psychic damage and be stunned until the start of Siren's next turn."},
  ["magicitem.siren-song-lyre.mot2014"]={title="Siren Song Lyre",subtitle="Item Magico - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou can use an action to play this lyre and cast one of the following spells from it: animal friendship, charm person, enthrall, suggestion. If the spell requires a saving throw, the spell save DC is 13.\n\nOnce the instrument has been used to cast a spell, it can't be used to cast that spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.sirene.mabjov2014"]={title="Sirene",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 147\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 63 (14d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 18 | CON 11 | INT 12 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe sirene can breathe air and water.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe sirene has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe sirene makes two Dagger attacks or two Shortbow attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw 6 to hit, range 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) cold damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nSirene's Song (2/Day)\n\nThe sirene casts suggestion with a range of 1 mile that affects all creatures of the sirene's choosing in range. Each target has disadvantage on the saving throw."},
  ["deity.sirrion.dsotdq2014"]={title="Sirrion",subtitle="Divindade - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 17\n\nPassionate and impulsive, Sirrion is the god of alchemy, transformation, serendipitous creation, and flames. He embodies momentary excitement, flaring quickly into fiery passion and smoldering long afterward. Sirrion's followers embrace extremes of emotion as forms of divine expression."},
  ["deity.sirrion.phb2014"]={title="Sirrion",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["creature.sivak-draconian.dsotdq2014"]={title="Sivak Draconian",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 199\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 57 (6d10 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 60\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 10 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Throes\n\nWhen the draconian is reduced to 0 hit points by a creature that is Large or smaller, the draconian crumbles into dust that then forms a spectral, shrieking image of the creature that killed it. The image lasts for 1 minute. Each creature hostile to the draconian within 10 feet of the image must succeed on a 14 Wisdom saving throw or be frightened of the spectral image for 1 minute. A frightened creature can repeat the saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe draconian makes two Serrated Sword attacks and one Tail attack.\n\nSerrated Sword\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d8 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d8 + 4) bludgeoning damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 14 Strength saving throw or be knocked prone.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nShape Theft\n\nAfter the draconian kills a Medium or smaller Humanoid, the draconian magically cloaks itself in an illusion to look and feel like that creature while retaining the draconian's game statistics (other than its size). This transformation lasts until the draconian dies or uses a bonus action to end it."},
  ["creature.sivis-scribe.efa2014"]={title="Sivis Scribe",subtitle="Criatura - EFA - 2014",body="Pagina: 84\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 56 (16d6)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 11 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 16 | WIS 12 | CHA 11\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Gnomish plus three other languages\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nWords of Reason\n\nAllies in a 10-foot XPHB originating from the scribe have XPHB on saving throws to avoid or end the XPHB or XPHB condition. This trait doesn't function if the scribe has the XPHB condition.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe scribe makes two Bursting Sigil attacks.\n\nBursting Sigil\n\nm,r 5, reach 5 ft. or range 60 ft. h13 (3d6 + 3) Radiant damage.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nWord of Stasis {@recharge 5}\n\ncon 13, each creature in a 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point the scribe can see within 60 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the start of the scribe's next turn. While the target is XPHB, its XPHB is 0 and can't increase."},
  ["creature.skaab.psi2014"]={title="Skaab",subtitle="Criatura - PSI - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.skabatha-nightshade.wbtw2014"]={title="Skabatha Nightshade",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 218\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 8\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 150 (20d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 9 | CON 16 | INT 12 | WIS 16 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Infernal, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nBoon of Immortality\n\nSkabatha is immune to any effect that would age her, and she can't die from old age.\n\nForgetfulness\n\nThe first creature that Skabatha sees after she finishes a long rest is invisible to her. She can't remember seeing the creature or perceive it using her truesight until the end of her next long rest.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSkabatha makes two Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h25 (6d6 + 4) poison damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nAlter Size\n\nSkabatha magically shrinks herself to Tiny size (between 4 and 8 inches tall) or returns to her normal size. If Skabatha lacks the room to return to her normal size, she attains the maximum size possible in the space available. Anything she is wearing or carrying changes size along with her.\n\nAs a Tiny creature, Skabatha deals 2 (1d4) poison damage when she hits with a Claw attack. She has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks, and disadvantage on Strength checks and Strength saving throws. Her statistics otherwise remain unchanged."},
  ["deity.skadi.phb2014"]={title="Skadi",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["creature.skeemo-weirdbottle.wdh2014"]={title="Skeemo Weirdbottle",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 72 (16d6 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 17 | WIS 12 | CHA 15\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Gnomish, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nGnome Cunning\n\nSkeemo has advantage on Intelligence, Wisdom, and Charisma saving throws against magic.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage. Or Ranged Weapon Attack: 5 to hit, range 20/60 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.skeletal-alchemist.gos2014"]={title="Skeletal Alchemist",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 253\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 11\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 13 | CON 15 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands all languages it knew in life but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe skeletal alchemist has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skeletal alchemist makes two Lob Acid attacks.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. one target. h4 (1d6 + 1) slashing damage.\n\nLob Acid\n\nrw 3 to hit, range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d8 + 1) acid damage."},
  ["creature.skeletal-bloodfin.crcotn2014"]={title="Skeletal Bloodfin",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 159\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead\n\nResistencias: piercing, slashing\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, deafened, frightened, paralyzed, poisoned"},
  ["creature.skeletal-giant-owl.imr2014"]={title="Skeletal Giant Owl",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned"},
  ["creature.skeletal-horror.aitfr-dn2014"]={title="Skeletal Horror",subtitle="Criatura - AitFR-DN - 2014",body="Pagina: 13\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 6\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 150 (20d10 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 10 | CHA 5\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe horror makes two attacks with its claws.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h19 (3d10 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nWave of Bones {@recharge 5}\n\nThe horror crashes into foes like a wave before quickly reforming. Each creature within 10 feet of the horror must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) bludgeoning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that fails this saving throw is also knocked prone."},
  ["creature.skeletal-juggernaut.gos2014"]={title="Skeletal Juggernaut",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 253\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 142 (19d10 + 38)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDisassemble\n\nIf the juggernaut is reduced to 0 hit points, twelve skeletons rise from its remains.\n\nFalling Apart\n\nIf the juggernaut does not have all of its hit points at the start of its turn, it loses 10 hit points.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe juggernaut makes two claws attacks.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h12 (2d8 + 3) slashing damage.\n\nAvalanche of Bones {@recharge 5}\n\nThe juggernaut collapses into a large heap before quickly reforming. Each creature within 10 feet of the juggernaut must make a 14 Dexterity saving throw, taking 18 (4d8) bludgeoning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature that fails this saving throw is also knocked prone."},
  ["creature.skeletal-knight.dsotdq2014"]={title="Skeletal Knight",subtitle="Criatura - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 10 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands the languages it knew in life but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nUndead Fortitude\n\nIf damage reduces the skeletal knight to 0 hit points, it must make a Constitution saving throw with a DC of 5 + the damage taken, unless the damage is bludgeoning or from a critical hit. On a success, the skeletal knight drops to 1 hit point instead.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe skeletal knight doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skeletal knight makes three Enervating Blade or Throwing Axe attacks in any combination.\n\nEnervating Blade\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h15 (3d6 + 5) necrotic damage, and if the target is a creature, it can't regain hit points until the start of the skeletal knight's next turn.\n\nThrowing Axe\n\nmw,rw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.skeletal-owlbear.imr2014"]={title="Skeletal Owlbear",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned"},
  ["creature.skeletal-polar-bear.imr2014"]={title="Skeletal Polar Bear",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned"},
  ["creature.skeletal-rats.bgdia2014"]={title="Skeletal Rats",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 23\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead"},
  ["creature.skeletal-riding-horse.dip2014"]={title="Skeletal Riding Horse",subtitle="Criatura - DIP - 2014",body="Pagina: 21\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead"},
  ["creature.skeletal-swarm.gos2014"]={title="Skeletal Swarm",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 254\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 60 (8d10 + 16)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: slashing, piercing\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned, prone, restrained, stunned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeafening Clatter\n\nCreatures are deafened while in the swarm's space.\n\nSwarm\n\nThe swarm can occupy another creature's space and vice versa, and the swarm can move through any opening large enough for a Small humanoid. The swarm can't regain hit points or gain temporary hit points.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlash\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 0 ft., one target in the swarm's space. h11 (2d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage if the swarm has half of its hit points or fewer."},
  ["creature.skeletal-two-headed-owlbear.imr2014"]={title="Skeletal Two-Headed Owlbear",subtitle="Criatura - IMR - 2014",body="Pagina: 36\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned"},
  ["species.skeleton.dmg2014"]={title="Skeleton",subtitle="Especie - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 282\n\nCreature Type\n\nYou are Undead.\n\nBrittle Bones\n\nYou are vulnerable to bludgeoning damage.\n\nUndead Nature\n\nYou are immune to poison damage and exhaustion, and you can't be poisoned. You don't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\nDarkvision\n\nYou can see in dim light within 60 feet of you as if it were bright light, and in darkness as if it were dim light. You can't discern color in darkness, only shades of gray.\n\nLanguages\n\nYou can't speak, but you can understand the languages you knew in life."},
  ["creature.skeleton.mm2014"]={title="Skeleton",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 272\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 13 (2d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands all languages it spoke in life but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nrw 4 to hit, range 80/320 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.skeleton.xmm2024"]={title="Skeleton",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 282\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 13 (2d8 + 4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 16 | CON 15 | INT 6 | WIS 8 | CHA 5\n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common plus one other language but can't speak\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: bludgeoning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nShortsword\n\nm 5, reach 5 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage.\n\nShortbow\n\nr 5, range 80/320 ft. h6 (1d6 + 3) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.skeleton-key.toa2014"]={title="Skeleton Key",subtitle="Criatura - ToA - 2014",body="Pagina: 126\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skeleton makes two dagger attacks.\n\nDagger\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.skeleton-lord.mabjov2014"]={title="Skeleton Lord",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 148\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 136 (16d8 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 18 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFear Aura\n\nAny creature hostile to the skeleton lord that starts its turn within 20 feet of the skeleton lord must make a 17 Wisdom saving throw, unless the skeleton lord is incapacitated. On a failed save, the creature has the frightened condition until the start of its next turn. If a creature's saving throw is successful, then the creature is immune to the skeleton lord's Fear Aura for the next 24 hours.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe skeleton lord has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe skeleton lord's weapon attacks are magical and gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls (included in the attack).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skeleton lord makes three Greatsword attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 10 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h13 (2d6 + 6) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.skeleton-warrior.mabjov2014"]={title="Skeleton Warrior",subtitle="Criatura - MaBJoV - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 90 (12d8 + 36)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 16 | WIS 12 | CHA 12\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: \n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe skeleton warrior has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nMagic Weapons\n\nThe skeleton warrior's weapon attacks are magical and gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls (included in the attack).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skeleton warrior makes two Greatsword attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h11 (2d6 + 4) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.sken-zabriss.egw2014"]={title="Sken Zabriss",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 11 | CON 15 | INT 13 | WIS 10 | CHA 12\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Giant\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nPowerful Build\n\nSken counts as one size larger when determining her carrying capacity and the weight she can push, drag, or lift.\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nSken wears a EGW. With it, she can cast the fog cloud spell centered on herself three times per day. The cloud lasts for 1 minute (no concentration required).\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) slashing damage, or 8 (1d10 + 3) slashing damage when used with two hands.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nStone's Endurance (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nWhen Sken takes damage, she can use her reaction to reduce the damage taken by 8 (1d12 + 2)."},
  ["deity.skerrit.phb2014"]={title="Skerrit",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["spell.skill-empowerment.xge2024"]={title="Skill Empowerment",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 165\n\nYour magic deepens a creature's understanding of its own talent. You touch one willing creature and give it expertise in one skill of your choice; until the spell ends, the creature doubles its proficiency bonus for ability checks it makes that use the chosen skill.\n\nYou must choose a skill in which the target is proficient and that isn't already benefiting from an effect, such as Expertise, that doubles its proficiency bonus."},
  ["feat.skill-expert.tce2014"]={title="Skill Expert",subtitle="Feat - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 80\n\nYou have honed your proficiency with particular skills, granting you the following benefits:\n\n• You gain proficiency in one phb of your choice.\n\n• Choose one skill in which you have proficiency. You gain expertise with that skill, which means your proficiency bonus is doubled for any ability check you make with it. The skill you choose must be one that isn't already benefiting from a feature, such as Expertise, that doubles your proficiency bonus."},
  ["feat.skill-expert.xphb2024"]={title="Skill Expert",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 207\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nSkill Proficiency\n\nYou gain proficiency in one skill of your choice.\n\nExpertise\n\nChoose one skill in which you have proficiency but lack XPHB. You gain XPHB with that skill."},
  ["feat.skilled.phb2014"]={title="Skilled",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 170\n\nYou gain proficiency in any combination of three phb or items of your choice."},
  ["feat.skilled.xphb2024"]={title="Skilled",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 201\n\nYou gain proficiency in any combination of three XPHB or items of your choice.\n\nRepeatable\n\nYou can take this feat more than once."},
  ["feature.skirmisher.xge2024.rogue.scout.3"]={title="Skirmisher",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 47\n\nStarting at 3rd level, you are difficult to pin down during a fight. You can move up to half your speed as a reaction when an enemy ends its turn within 5 feet of you. This movement doesn't provoke opportunity attacks."},
  ["creature.skittering-horror.ggr2014"]={title="Skittering Horror",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 205\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / H\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 228 (24d12 + 72)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, climb: 40\n\nSTR 22 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 2 | WIS 14 | CHA 18\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nVulnerabilidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe horror can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the horror has disadvantage on attack rolls and on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe horror can use its Maddening Presence and make three attacks: one with its bite and two with its claws.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h28 (4d10 + 6) piercing damage.\n\nClaws\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h24 (4d8 + 6) slashing damage.\n\nMaddening Presence\n\nThe horror targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see or hear the horror, the target must make a 17 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed saving throw, the target becomes paralyzed until the end of its next turn. If a creature's saving throw is successful, the creature is immune to the horror's Maddening Presence for the next 24 hours."},
  ["creature.skitterwidget.cm2014"]={title="Skitterwidget",subtitle="Criatura - CM - 2014",body="Pagina: 136\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 85 (10d8 + 40)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Skitterwidget\n\nImunidades: lightning, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, exhaustion, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLightning Absorption\n\nWhenever the skitterwidget is subjected to lightning damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the lightning damage dealt.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe skitterwidget doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skitterwidget makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its tail.\n\nBite\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d6 + 3) piercing damage. If the target is a creature, it is grappled by the skitterwidget (escape 13).\n\nTail\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 10 (3d6) lightning damage, and if the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be stunned until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nGood Parent\n\nThe skitterwidget imposes disadvantage on one attack roll made against a kiddywidget it can see within 5 feet of it."},
  ["deity.skoraeus-stonebones.phb2014"]={title="Skoraeus Stonebones",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 296"},
  ["creature.skr-a-s-orsk.egw2014"]={title="Skr'a S'orsk",subtitle="Criatura - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 254\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting (Lizardfolk Form Only)"},
  ["creature.skriss.oota2014"]={title="Skriss",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 18"},
  ["creature.skulk.mpmm2014"]={title="Skulk",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 18 (4d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 19 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 7 | CHA 1\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFallible Invisibility\n\nThe skulk is invisible. This invisibility can be circumvented by three things:\n\n• Charnel Candles The skulk appears as a dim, translucent form in the light of a candle made of fat rendered from a corpse whose identity is unknown.\n\n• Children Humanoid children, aged 10 and under, can see through this invisibility.\n\n• Reflective Surfaces The skulk appears as a drab, smooth-skinned biped if its reflection can be seen in a mirror or on another surface.\n\nTrackless\n\nThe skulk leaves no tracks to indicate where it has been or where it's headed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) slashing damage plus 3 (1d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["creature.skulk.mtf2014"]={title="Skulk",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 227\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 18 (4d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 19 | CON 10 | INT 10 | WIS 7 | CHA 1\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Common but can't speak\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFallible Invisibility\n\nThe skulk is invisible. This invisibility can be circumvented by three things:\n\n• The skulk appears as a drab, smooth-skinned humanoid if its reflection can be seen in a mirror or on another surface.\n\n• The skulk appears as a dim, translucent form in the light of a candle made of fat rendered from a corpse whose identity is unknown.\n\n• Humanoid children, aged 10 and under, can see through this invisibility.\n\nTrackless\n\nThe skulk leaves no tracks to indicate where it has been or where it's headed.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d4 + 4) slashing damage. If the skulk has advantage on the attack roll, the target also takes 7 (2d6) necrotic damage."},
  ["feat.skulker.phb2014"]={title="Skulker",subtitle="Feat - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 170\n\nYou are expert at slinking through shadows. You gain the following benefits:\n\n• You can try to hide when you are lightly obscured from the creature from which you are hiding.\n\n• When you are hidden from a creature and miss it with a ranged weapon attack, making the attack doesn't reveal your position.\n\n• Dim light doesn't impose disadvantage on your Wisdom (Perception) checks relying on sight."},
  ["feat.skulker.xphb2024"]={title="Skulker",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 208\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nBlindsight\n\nYou have XPHB with a range of 10 feet.\n\nFog of War\n\nYou exploit the distractions of battle, gaining XPHB on any Dexterity (XPHB) check you make as part of the XPHB action during combat.\n\nSniper\n\nIf you make an attack roll while hidden and the roll misses, making the attack roll doesn't reveal your location."},
  ["magicitem.skull-card.bmt2014"]={title="Skull Card",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nAs an action, you can brandish this card and use it to cast BMT as a 6th-level spell (spell attack bonus 9, save 17). Once this property is used, it can't be used again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.skull-flier.slw2014"]={title="Skull Flier",subtitle="Criatura - SLW - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 24 (3d8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 50\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 10 | INT 1 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, psychic\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSting\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, and the target must make a 11 Constitution saving throw, taking 10 (3d6) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. If the poison damage reduces the target to 0 hit points, the target is stable but poisoned for 1 hour, even after regaining hit points, and is paralyzed while poisoned in this way."},
  ["magicitem.skull-helm.bmt2014"]={title="Skull Helm",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 38\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nWhile wearing this skull-shaped helm, you have resistance to cold, poison, and necrotic damage.\n\nAdditionally, while wearing the helm, you can cast BMT from it without requiring material components. Once you use the helm to cast the spell, the helm can't cast this spell again until the next dawn."},
  ["creature.skull-lasher-of-myrkul.bgdia2014"]={title="Skull Lasher of Myrkul",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 234\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 10 | DEX 14 | CON 15 | INT 16 | WIS 13 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Infernal\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skull lasher makes two attacks with its flail.\n\nIron Skull Flail\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d8) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) necrotic damage, and the target has disadvantage on all saving throws until the end of the skull lasher's next turn.\n\nRay of Sickness (1st-Level Spell; Requires a Spell Slot)\n\nrs 5 to hit, range 60 ft., one creature. h9 (2d8) poison damage, and the target must succeed on a 13 Constitution saving throw or be poisoned until the end of the skull lasher's next turn. If the skull lasher casts this spell using a spell slot of 2nd level or higher, the damage increases by 1d8 for each slot level above 1st."},
  ["creature.skull-lord.mpmm2014"]={title="Skull Lord",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 112 (15d8 + 45)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nEvasion\n\nIf the skull lord is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half the damage, the skull lord instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the saving throw and only half damage if it fails, provided it isn't incapacitated.\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the skull lord fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMaster of the Grave\n\nWhile within 30 feet of the skull lord, any Undead ally of the skull lord makes saving throws with advantage, and that ally regains 1d6 hit points whenever it starts its turn there.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe skull lord doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skull lord makes three Bone Staff or Deathly Ray attacks.\n\nBone Staff\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 21 (6d6) necrotic damage.\n\nDeathly Ray\n\nrs 10 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h27 (5d8 + 5) necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nAttack\n\nThe skull lord makes one Bone Staff or Deathly Ray attack.\n\nMove\n\nThe skull lord moves up to its speed without provoking opportunity attack.\n\nSummon Undead (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe skull lord summons up to five skeleton or zombie in unoccupied spaces within 30 feet of it. They remain until destroyed. Undead summoned in this way roll initiative, act in the next available turn, and obey the skull lord. The skull lord can have no more than five Undead summoned by this ability at a time."},
  ["creature.skull-lord.mtf2014"]={title="Skull Lord",subtitle="Criatura - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 230\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: undead / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 105 (14d8 + 42)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 16 | CON 17 | INT 16 | WIS 15 | CHA 21\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all the languages it knew in life\n\nResistencias: cold, necrotic\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf the skull lord fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMaster of the Grave\n\nWhile within 30 feet of the skull lord, any undead ally of the skull lord makes saving throws with advantage, and that ally regains 1d6 hit points whenever it starts its turn there.\n\nEvasion\n\nIf the skull lord is subjected to an effect that allows it to make a Dexterity saving throw to take only half the damage, the skull lord instead takes no damage if it succeeds on the saving throw, and only half damage if it fails.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skull lord makes three bone staff attacks.\n\nBone Staff\n\nmw 8 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d8 + 3) bludgeoning damage plus 14 (4d6) necrotic damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBone Staff (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe skull lord makes a bone staff attack.\n\nCantrip\n\nThe skull lord casts a cantrip.\n\nMove\n\nThe skull lord moves up to its speed without provoking opportunity attacks.\n\nSummon Undead (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nUp to five skeleton or zombie appear in unoccupied spaces within 30 feet of the skull lord and remain until destroyed. Undead summoned in this way roll initiative and act in the next available turn. The skull lord can have up to five undead summoned by this ability at a time."},
  ["magicitem.skull-of-selfish-knowledge.coa2014"]={title="Skull of Selfish Knowledge",subtitle="Item Magico - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 269\n\nRaridade: rare\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 4000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 2000 PO / 50 dias\n\nYou may use an action to make the magical skull devour a nonmagical book, map, or scroll. Once devoured the learning is forever available to you, but you can never write the information down or communicate it to others. It is for you alone."},
  ["creature.skum.gos2014"]={title="Skum",subtitle="Criatura - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 254\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 93 (11d8 + 44)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 40\n\nSTR 19 | DEX 11 | CON 18 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 9\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Deep Speech, telepathy 60 ft.\n\nResistencias: psychic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAbolethic Vassal\n\nThe skum is permanently charmed by its aboleth master.\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe skum can breathe air and water.\n\nPsychic Conditioning\n\nThe skum is immune to the frightened and charmed conditions unless they are from effects created by an aboleth.\n\nWater Dependency\n\nThe skum takes 6 (1d12) acid damage every 10 minutes it goes without exposure to water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skum makes three attacks: two with its trident and one with its Mind-Breaking Touch.\n\nTrident\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) piercing damage.\n\nMind-Breaking Touch\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h18 (4d8) psychic damage, and the target has disadvantage on Wisdom saving throws until the end of the skum's next turn."},
  ["creature.sky-leviathan.psk2014"]={title="Sky Leviathan",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: beast / G\n\nCR: 10\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 247 (15d20 + 90)\n\nDeslocamento: fly: 50\n\nSTR 28 | DEX 7 | CON 22 | INT 1 | WIS 8 | CHA 4\n\nSalvamentos: \n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (3d8 + 9) piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 18 Dexterity saving throw or be swallowed by the leviathan. A swallowed creature is blinded and restrained, it has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the leviathan, and it takes 21 (6d6) acid damage at the start of each of the leviathan's turns.\n\nIf the leviathan takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, the leviathan must succeed on a 21 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, which fall prone in a space within 10 feet of the leviathan. If the leviathan dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse by using 20 feet of movement, exiting prone."},
  ["creature.sky-whale.psk2014"]={title="Sky Whale",subtitle="Criatura - PSK - 2014",body="Pagina: 28\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: fly: 50"},
  ["magicitem.skyblinder-staff.ggr2014"]={title="Skyblinder Staff",subtitle="Item Magico - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 181\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nYou gain a +1 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic quarterstaff. While holding it, you gain a +1 bonus to spell attack rolls.\n\nIf a flying creature you can see within 30 feet of you makes an attack roll against you, you can use your reaction to hold the staff aloft and cause it to flare with light. The attacker has disadvantage on the attack roll, and it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be blinded until the start of its next turn."},
  ["creature.skyjek-roc.ggr2014"]={title="Skyjek Roc",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 219\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / L\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 37 (5d10 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 90\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 3 | WIS 10 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nKeen Sight\n\nThe roc has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe roc makes two attacks: one with its beak and one with its talons.\n\nBeak\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nTalons\n\nmw 7 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h10 (2d4 + 5) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.skylla.wbtw2014"]={title="Skylla",subtitle="Criatura - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 10\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 9 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 12 | WIS 15 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nSkylla carries an WBtW (see appendix A) with 10 charges. The staff regains 1d6 + 4 expended charges daily at dawn. If its last charge is expended, roll a d20; on a 1, the staff is destroyed.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSkylla makes two Eldritch Staff attacks. She can replace one of the attacks with a use of Spellcasting.\n\nEldritch Staff\n\nmw 2 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage, or 4 (1d8) bludgeoning damage when used with two hands, and Skylla can expend up to 3 of the staff's charges, dealing an extra 4 (1d8) lightning damage for each expended charge.\n\n=== REACOES ===\n\nEldritch Escape\n\nWhen Skylla takes damage, she can expend 3 charges of her eldritch staff to turn invisible and teleport, along with any equipment she's wearing or carrying, up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space she can see. She remains invisible until the start of her next turn or until she attacks or casts a spell."},
  ["item.skyship.egw2014"]={title="Skyship",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 72\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.skyswimmer.ggr2014"]={title="Skyswimmer",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 220\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / G\n\nCR: 13\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 216 (16d20 + 48)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10, fly: 60\n\nSTR 23 | DEX 15 | CON 16 | INT 7 | WIS 12 | CHA 6\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe skyswimmer can breathe air and water.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe skyswimmer makes three attacks: one with its bite and two with its slam.\n\nBite\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h22 (3d10 + 6) piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature, it must succeed on a 19 Dexterity saving throw or be swallowed by the skyswimmer. A swallowed creature is blinded and restrained, it has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the skyswimmer, and it takes 21 (6d6) acid damage at the start of each of the skyswimmer's turns. If the skyswimmer takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from the swallowed creature, the skyswimmer must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate the creature, which falls prone in a space within 10 feet of the skyswimmer. If the skyswimmer dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse by using 15 feet of movement, exiting prone.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 11 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h19 (2d12 + 6) bludgeoning damage."},
  ["creature.skyweaver.pota2014"]={title="Skyweaver",subtitle="Criatura - PotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 12/15\n\nPV: 44 (8d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 10 | CHA 16\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Auran, Common\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage."},
  ["spell.skywrite.xge2024"]={title="Skywrite",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 165\n\nYou cause up to ten words to form in a part of the sky you can see. The words appear to be made of cloud and remain in place for the spell's duration. The words dissipate when the spell ends. A strong wind can disperse the clouds and end the spell early."},
  ["language.slaad.mm2014"]={title="Slaad",subtitle="Idioma - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 276"},
  ["language.slaad.xmm2024"]={title="Slaad",subtitle="Idioma - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 285"},
  ["charoption.slaad-host.idrotf2014"]={title="Slaad Host",subtitle="Opcao de Personagem - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 264\n\nA red slaad implanted a pellet-sized egg in me shortly before I started my adventuring career. If I can't get rid of it in the next two months, the egg will gestate inside me, and a slaad tadpole will burst from my chest, killing me. It will then quickly grow into an adult slaad and kill even more people."},
  ["creature.slaad-tadpole.mm2014"]={title="Slaad Tadpole",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / T\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 10 (4d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 5 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Slaad but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h4 (1d4 + 2) piercing damage."},
  ["creature.slaad-tadpole.xmm2024"]={title="Slaad Tadpole",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 284\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / T\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 7 (3d4)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, burrow: 10\n\nSTR 7 | DEX 15 | CON 10 | INT 3 | WIS 5 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Slaad but can't speak\n\nResistencias: acid, cold, fire, lightning, thunder\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe slaad has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nBite\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h5 (1d6 + 2) Piercing damage."},
  ["creature.sladis-vadir.oota2014"]={title="Sladis Vadir",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.slarkrethel.skt2014"]={title="Slarkrethel",subtitle="Criatura - SKT - 2014",body="Pagina: 224\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / G\n\nCR: 25\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 472 (27d20 + 189)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, swim: 60\n\nSTR 30 | DEX 11 | CON 25 | INT 22 | WIS 18 | CHA 20\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands Abyssal, Celestial, Infernal, and Primordial but can't speak, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: lightning\n\nImunidades a condicoes: frightened, paralyzed\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nLegendary Resistance (3/Day)\n\nIf Slarkrethel fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nAmphibious\n\nSlarkrethel can breathe air and water.\n\nFreedom of Movement\n\nSlarkrethel ignores difficult terrain, and magical effects can't reduce its speed or cause it to be restrained. It can spend 5 feet of movement to escape from nonmagical restraints or being grappled.\n\nSiege Monster\n\nSlarkrethel deals double damage to objects and structures.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSlarkrethel makes three tentacle attacks, each of which it can replace with one use of Fling.\n\nBite\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h23 (3d8 + 10) piercing damage. If the target is a Large or smaller creature grappled by Slarkrethel, that creature is swallowed, and the grapple ends. While swallowed, the creature is blinded and restrained, it has Cover against attacks and other effects outside Slarkrethel, and it takes 42 (12d6) acid damage at the start of each of Slarkrethel's turns. If Slarkrethel takes 50 damage or more on a single turn from a creature inside it, Slarkrethel must succeed on a 25 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate all swallowed creatures, which fall prone in a space within 10 feet of Slarkrethel. If Slarkrethel dies, a swallowed creature is no longer restrained by it and can escape from the corpse using 15 feet of movement, exiting prone.\n\nTentacle\n\nmw 17 to hit, reach 30 ft., one target. h20 (3d6 + 10) bludgeoning damage, and the target is grappled (escape 18). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained. Slarkrethel has ten tentacles, each of which can grapple one target.\n\nFling\n\nOne Large or smaller object held or creature grappled by Slarkrethel is thrown up to 60 feet in a random direction and knocked prone. If a thrown target strikes a solid surface, the target takes 3 (1d6) bludgeoning damage for every 10 feet it was thrown. If the target is thrown at another creature, that creature must succeed on a 18 Dexterity saving throw or take the same damage and be knocked prone.\n\nLightning Storm\n\nSlarkrethel magically creates three bolts of lightning, each of which can strike a target Slarkrethel can see within 120 feet of it. A target must make a 23 Dexterity saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) lightning damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTentacle Attack or Fling\n\nSlarkrethel makes one tentacle attack or uses its Fling.\n\nLightning Storm (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nSlarkrethel uses Lightning Storm.\n\nInk Cloud (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nWhile underwater, Slarkrethel expels an ink cloud in a 60-foot radius. The cloud spreads around corners, and that area is Vision and Light to creatures other than Slarkrethel. Each creature other than Slarkrethel that ends its turn there must succeed on a 23 Constitution saving throw, taking 16 (3d10) poison damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one. A strong current disperses the cloud, which otherwise disappears at the end of Slarkrethel's next turn."},
  ["feat.slasher.tce2014"]={title="Slasher",subtitle="Feat - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 81\n\nYou've learned where to cut to have the greatest results, granting you the following benefits:\n\n• Once per turn when you hit a creature with an attack that deals slashing damage, you can reduce the speed of the target by 10 feet until the start of your next turn.\n\n• When you score a critical hit that deals slashing damage to a creature, you grievously wound it. Until the start of your next turn, the target has disadvantage on all attack rolls."},
  ["feat.slasher.xphb2024"]={title="Slasher",subtitle="Feat - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 208\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nHamstring\n\nOnce per turn when you hit a creature with an attack that deals Slashing damage, you can reduce the XPHB of that creature by 10 feet until the start of your next turn.\n\nEnhanced Critical\n\nWhen you score a XPHB that deals Slashing damage to a creature, it has XPHB on attack rolls until the start of your next turn."},
  ["feature.slashing-flourish.xge2024.bard.swords.3"]={title="Slashing Flourish",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 15\n\nYou can expend one use of your Bardic Inspiration to cause the weapon to deal extra damage to the target you hit and to any other creature of your choice that you can see within 5 feet of you. The damage equals the number you roll on the Bardic Inspiration die."},
  ["creature.slayer.coa2014"]={title="Slayer",subtitle="Criatura - CoA - 2014",body="Pagina: 30\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fiend / M\n\nCR: 12\n\nCA: 19\n\nPV: 136 (16d8 + 64)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 19 | CON 18 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Languages of the host\n\nResistencias: \n\nImunidades: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAssassinate\n\nDuring its first turn, the Slayer has advantage on attack rolls against any creature that hasn't taken a turn. Any hit the Slayer scores against a surprised creature is a critical hit.\n\nDevil's Sight\n\nMagical darkness doesn't impede the Slayer's darkvision.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe Slayer has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe Slayer makes four Claw attacks.\n\nClaw\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (2d6 + 5) slashing damage plus 7 (2d6) poison damage. The Slayer deals an extra 14 (4d6) slashing damage when it has advantage on the attack roll and hits the target."},
  ["feature.slayer-s-counter.xge2024.ranger.monster-slayer.15"]={title="Slayer's Counter",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 43\n\nAt 15th level, you gain the ability to counterattack when your prey tries to sabotage you. If the target of your Slayer's Prey forces you to make a saving throw, you can use your reaction to make one weapon attack against the quarry. You make this attack immediately before making the saving throw. If your attack hits, your save automatically succeeds, in addition to the attack's normal effects."},
  ["feature.slayer-s-prey.xge2024.ranger.monster-slayer.3"]={title="Slayer's Prey",subtitle="Caracteristica - XGE - 2024",body=""},
  ["item.sled.phb2014"]={title="Sled",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 157\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.sled.xphb2024"]={title="Sled",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 230\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.sled-dog.frhof2014"]={title="Sled Dog",subtitle="Item - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 132\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA sled dog uses the XMM stat block (see the Monster Manual). A sled dog pulling a sled alone must take a XPHB after pulling a sled for 1 hour; otherwise, it gains 1 XPHB level."},
  ["item.sled-dog.idrotf2014"]={title="Sled Dog",subtitle="Item - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA sled dog (use the wolf stat block in appendix A of the Monster Manual) costs 50 gp and can pull 360 pounds.\n\nSled dogs must take a short rest after pulling a sled for 1 hour; otherwise, they gain one level of exhaustion."},
  ["creature.sled-dog.rot2014"]={title="Sled Dog",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.sledgehammer.phb2014"]={title="Sledgehammer",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["spell.sleep.phb2014"]={title="Sleep",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\nThis spell sends creatures into a magical slumber. Roll 5d8; the total is how many hit points of creatures this spell can affect. Creatures within 20 feet of a point you choose within range are affected in ascending order of their current hit points (ignoring unconscious creatures).\n\nStarting with the creature that has the lowest current hit points, each creature affected by this spell falls unconscious until the spell ends, the sleeper takes damage, or someone uses an action to shake or slap the sleeper awake. Subtract each creature's hit points from the total before moving on to the creature with the next lowest hit points. A creature's hit points must be equal to or less than the remaining total for that creature to be affected.\n\nUndead and creatures immune to being charmed aren't affected by this spell."},
  ["spell.sleep.xphb2024"]={title="Sleep",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 317\n\nEach creature of your choice in a 5-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point within range must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or have the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn, at which point it must repeat the save. If the target fails the second save, the target has the XPHB condition for the duration. The spell ends on a target if it takes damage or someone within 5 feet of it takes an action to shake it out of the spell's effect.\n\nCreatures that don't sleep, such as elves, or that have XPHB to the XPHB condition automatically succeed on saves against this spell."},
  ["item.sleep-grenade.qftis2014"]={title="Sleep Grenade",subtitle="Item - QftIS - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nRaridade: none\n\n{#itemEntry Grenade|DMG\n\nThis grenade releases a cloud of soporific mist that fills a 20-foot-radius sphere, then dissipates. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or have the unconscious condition for 1 hour. The condition ends on a creature early if the creature takes damage or if another creature uses an action to shake it awake."},
  ["traphazard.sleep-of-ages-trap.xge2024"]={title="Sleep of Ages Trap",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 114\n\nWhen a sleep of ages trap activates, a pressure plate unleashes a spell that threatens to send intruders into a deep slumber. The dungeon's guardians can then more easily dispose of the sleepers."},
  ["spell.sleet-storm.phb2014"]={title="Sleet Storm",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 276\n\nUntil the spell ends, freezing rain and sleet fall in a 20-foot-tall cylinder with a 40-foot radius centered on a point you choose within range. The area is PHB, and exposed flames in the area are doused.\n\nThe ground in the area is covered with slick ice, making it difficult terrain. When a creature enters the spell's area for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it must make a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, it falls prone.\n\nIf a creature starts its turn in the spell's area and is concentration on a spell, the creature must make a successful Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC or lose concentration."},
  ["spell.sleet-storm.xphb2024"]={title="Sleet Storm",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 317\n\nUntil the spell ends, sleet falls in a 40-foot-tall, 20-foot-radius XPHB centered on a point you choose within range. The area is XPHB, and exposed flames in the area are doused.\n\nGround in the XPHB is XPHB. When a creature enters the XPHB for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there, it must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition and lose XPHB."},
  ["item.sling.phb2014"]={title="Sling",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 149\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.sling.xphb2024"]={title="Sling",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 215\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.sling-bullet.phb2014"]={title="Sling Bullet",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.sling-bullet.xphb2024"]={title="Sling Bullet",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSling bullets are used with a weapon that has the ammunition property to make a ranged attack. Each time you attack with the weapon, you expend one piece of ammunition. Drawing the ammunition from a quiver, case, or other container is part of the attack (you need a free hand to load a one-handed weapon). At the end of the battle, you can recover half your expended ammunition by taking a minute to search the battlefield.\n\nSling Bullets are typically stored in a XPHB (bought separately)."},
  ["item.sling-bullets-20.phb2014"]={title="Sling Bullets (20)",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.sling-bullets-20.xphb2024"]={title="Sling Bullets (20)",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 222\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSling bullets are used with a weapon that has the ammunition property to make a ranged attack. Each time you attack with the weapon, you expend one piece of ammunition. Drawing the ammunition from a quiver, case, or other container is part of the attack (you need a free hand to load a one-handed weapon). At the end of the battle, you can recover half your expended ammunition by taking a minute to search the battlefield.\n\nSling Bullets are typically stored in a XPHB (bought separately)."},
  ["magicitem.sling-bullets-of-althemone.mot2014"]={title="Sling Bullets of Althemone",subtitle="Item Magico - MOT - 2014",body="Pagina: 198\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias\n\nThe sling bullets come in a pouch, which contains 1d4 + 4 bullets. Roll on the Magic Sling Bullets table for each bullet to determine its magical property.\n\nYou have a +2 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with each of these bullets. If a bullet misses its target, the bullet teleports back into the pouch. Once a bullet hits a target, the bullet loses its magic.\n\nd4 | Bullet\n\n1 | Banishment. A creature that takes damage from this bullet must succeed on a 15 Charisma saving throw or be banished as though affected by the banishment spell.\n\n2 | Fulguration. On a hit, this bullet deals an extra 2d8 lightning damage to its target. All other creatures within 10 feet of the target must each succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or take 1d8 thunder damage.\n\n3 | Stunning. On a hit, this bullet deals an extra 1d10 force damage, and the target is stunned until the end of your next turn.\n\n4 | Tracking. A creature that takes damage from this bullet is marked with a glowing rune where the bullet hit. The mark lasts 24 hours. While the creature is marked, you always know the direction to it."},
  ["magicitem.sling-of-giant-felling.bmt2014"]={title="Sling of Giant Felling",subtitle="Item Magico - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 68\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhen you hit a Giant creature with a ranged attack roll using this magic sling, the creature must succeed on a 18 Constitution saving throw or have the prone condition."},
  ["magicitem.slippers-of-spider-climbing.dmg2014"]={title="Slippers of Spider Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 200\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these light shoes, you can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and upside down along ceilings, while leaving your hands free. You have a climbing speed equal to your walking speed. However, the slippers don't allow you to move this way on a slippery surface, such as one covered by ice or oil."},
  ["magicitem.slippers-of-spider-climbing.xdmg2024"]={title="Slippers of Spider Climbing",subtitle="Item Magico - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 304\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nWhile you wear these light shoes, you can move up, down, and across vertical surfaces and along ceilings, while leaving your hands free. You have a XPHB equal to your XPHB. However, the slippers don't allow you to move this way on a slippery surface, such as one covered by ice or oil."},
  ["traphazard.slippery-ice.dmg2014"]={title="Slippery Ice",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 110\n\nSlippery ice is difficult terrain. When a creature moves onto slippery ice for the first time on a turn, it must succeed on a 10 Dexterity (Acrobatics) check or fall prone."},
  ["traphazard.slippery-ice.xdmg2024"]={title="Slippery Ice",subtitle="Armadilha/Perigo - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 69\n\nSlippery ice is XPHB. A creature that moves onto slippery ice for the first time on a turn or starts its turn there must succeed on a 10 Dexterity saving throw or have the XPHB condition."},
  ["feature.slippery-mind.phb2014.rogue.base.15"]={title="Slippery Mind",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.slippery-mind.xphb2024.rogue.base.15"]={title="Slippery Mind",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.slithering-bloodfin.crcotn2014"]={title="Slithering Bloodfin",subtitle="Criatura - CRCotN - 2014",body="Pagina: 209\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: aberration / L\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 93 (11d10 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 5, swim: 50\n\nSTR 20 | DEX 14 | CON 16 | INT 2 | WIS 10 | CHA 3\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 100 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nWhen the bloodfin dies, it explodes in a cloud of toxic blood. Each creature in a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on the exploding bloodfin, including any creature swallowed by the bloodfin, must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or take 10 (3d6) poison damage. A creature inside the bloodfin when it explodes falls prone in the space formerly occupied by the bloodfin and is no longer blinded or restrained by it.\n\nWater Breathing\n\nThe bloodfin can breathe only underwater.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe bloodfin makes one Bite attack and one Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit (with advantage if the target is a creature missing any hit points), reach 5 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) piercing damage, and if the target is a creature, it is grappled (escape 15). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained, and the bloodfin can't bite another target.\n\nTail\n\nmw 9 to hit (with advantage if the target is a creature missing any hit points), reach 10 ft., one target. h19 (4d6 + 5) bludgeoning damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSwallow\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one Medium or smaller creature the bloodfin is grappling. hThe bloodfin swallows the target. The swallowed creature is no longer grappled but is blinded and restrained. It has Cover against attacks and other effects outside the bloodfin, it takes 14 (4d6) necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns, and the bloodfin regains hit points equal to the necrotic damage dealt. A bloodfin can have only one creature swallowed at a time.\n\nIf the bloodfin takes 30 damage or more on a single turn from the swallowed creature, the bloodfin must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw at the end of that turn or regurgitate the creature, which falls prone in a space within 5 feet of the bloodfin and is no longer blinded or restrained by it."},
  ["creature.slithering-tracker.mpmm2014"]={title="Slithering Tracker",subtitle="Criatura - MPMM - 2014",body="Pagina: 221\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 19 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands languages it knew in its previous form but can't speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nVulnerabilidades: cold, fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nIf the slithering tracker is motionless at the start of combat, it has advantage on its initiative roll. Moreover, if a creature hasn't observed the slithering tracker move or act, that creature must succeed on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check to discern that the slithering tracker isn't a puddle.\n\nLiquid Form\n\nThe slithering tracker can enter an enemy's space and stop there. It can also move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe slithering tracker can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nLife Leech\n\nOne Large or smaller creature that the slithering tracker can see within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or be grappled (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained and unable to breathe unless it can breathe water. In addition, the grappled target takes 16 (3d10) necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns. The slithering tracker can grapple only one target at a time.\n\nWhile grappling the target, the slithering tracker takes only half any damage dealt to it (rounded down), and the target takes the other half.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nWatery Stealth\n\nIf underwater, the slithering tracker takes the Hide action, and it makes the Dexterity (Stealth) check with advantage."},
  ["creature.slithering-tracker.vgm2014"]={title="Slithering Tracker",subtitle="Criatura - VGM - 2014",body="Pagina: 191\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: ooze / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 32 (5d8 + 10)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, climb: 30, swim: 30\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 19 | CON 15 | INT 10 | WIS 14 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: blindsight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: understands languages it knew in its previous form but can't speak\n\nResistencias: \n\nVulnerabilidades: cold, fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, deafened, exhaustion, grappled, paralyzed, petrified, prone, restrained, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmbusher\n\nIn the first round of a combat, the slithering tracker has advantage on attack rolls against any creature it surprised.\n\nDamage Transfer\n\nWhile grappling a creature, the slithering tracker takes only haIf the damage dealt to it, and the creature it is grappling takes the other half.\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nWhile the slithering tracker remains motionless, it is indistinguishable from a puddle, unless an observer succeeds on a 18 Intelligence (Investigation) check.\n\nKeen Tracker\n\nThe slithering tracker has advantage on Wisdom checks to track prey.\n\nLiquid Form\n\nThe slithering tracker can enter an enemy's space and stop there. It can also move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nSpider Climb\n\nThe slithering tracker can climb difficult surfaces, including upside down on ceilings, without needing to make an ability check.\n\nWatery Stealth\n\nWhile underwater, the slithering tracker has advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks made to hide, and it can take the Hide action as a bonus action.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nSlam\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h8 (1d10 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nLife Leech\n\nOne Large or smaller creature that the slithering tracker can see within 5 feet of it must succeed on a 13 Dexterity saving throw or be grappled (escape 13). Until this grapple ends, the target is restrained and unable to breathe unless it can breathe water. In addition, the grappled target takes 16 (3d10) necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns. The slithering tracker can grapple only one target at a time."},
  ["creature.sloopidoop.oota2014"]={title="Sloopidoop",subtitle="Criatura - OotA - 2014",body="Pagina: 29\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nINT 18"},
  ["spell.slow.phb2014"]={title="Slow",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 277\n\nYou alter time around up to six creatures of your choice in a 40-foot cube within range. Each target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be affected by this spell for the duration.\n\nAn affected target's speed is halved, it takes a −2 penalty to AC and Dexterity saving throws, and it can't use reactions. On its turn, it can use either an action or a bonus action, not both. Regardless of the creature's abilities or magic items, it can't make more than one melee or ranged attack during its turn.\n\nIf the creature attempts to cast a spell with a casting time of 1 action, roll a d20. On an 11 or higher, the spell doesn't take effect until the creature's next turn, and the creature must use its action on that turn to complete the spell. If it can't, the spell is wasted.\n\nA creature affected by this spell makes another Wisdom saving throw at the end of each of its turns. On a successful save, the effect ends for it."},
  ["spell.slow.xphb2024"]={title="Slow",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 3 - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 318\n\nYou alter time around up to six creatures of your choice in a 40-foot XPHB within range. Each target must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be affected by this spell for the duration.\n\nAn affected target's XPHB is halved, it takes a -2 penalty to AC and Dexterity saving throws, and it can't take Reactions. On its turns, it can take either an action or a XPHB, not both, and it can make only one attack if it takes the XPHB action. If it casts a spell with a Somatic component, there is a 25 chance the spell fails as a result of the target making the spell's gestures too slowly.\n\nAn affected target repeats the save at the end of each of its turns, ending the spell on itself on a success."},
  ["feature.slow-fall.phb2014.monk.base.4"]={title="Slow Fall",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nBeginning at 4th level, you can use your reaction when you fall to reduce any falling damage you take by an amount equal to five times your monk level."},
  ["feature.slow-fall.xphb2024.monk.base.4"]={title="Slow Fall",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["creature.sludge-hag.mgelft2014"]={title="Sludge Hag",subtitle="Criatura - MGELFT - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 17\n\nPV: 82 (11d8 + 33)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 12 | CON 16 | INT 13 | WIS 14 | CHA 14\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Draconic, Sylvan\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmorphous\n\nThe sludge hag can move through a space as narrow as 1 inch wide without squeezing.\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe sludge hag can breathe air and water.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nFalse Appearance\n\nThe sludge hag collapses into a oily pool of sludge. While motionless, the sludge hag is indistinguishable from any other oily pool of oozy drippiness.\n\nSludge Slap\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h12 (1d8 + 8) bludgeoning damage, plus 4 (1d8) acid damage. Sludge Slap does both bludgeoning and acid damage."},
  ["magicitem.slumbering-dragon-vessel.ftd2014"]={title="Slumbering Dragon Vessel",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis vessel can be a potion bottle, drinking horn, or other container meant to hold a liquid.\n\nAs a bonus action, if the vessel is empty, you can speak the command word to fill the vessel with one of the following (your choice): ale, olive oil, a potion of healing, or a potion of climbing. Once this property is used, it can't be used until the next dawn. A potion you create in this way loses its magical properties if it isn't imbibed within 24 hours."},
  ["magicitem.slumbering-dragon-touched-focus.ftd2014"]={title="Slumbering Dragon-Touched Focus",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 26\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis wondrous item can be a scepter, an orb, an amulet, a crystal, or another finely crafted object. It typically incorporates imagery of dragons' wings, claws, teeth, or scales.\n\nYou have advantage on initiative rolls. While you are holding the focus, it can function as a spellcasting focus for all your spells."},
  ["magicitem.slumbering-scaled-ornament.ftd2014"]={title="Slumbering Scaled Ornament",subtitle="Item Magico - FTD - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nThis ornament can be jewelry, a cloak, or another wearable accessory. It appears to be fashioned from a dragon's scale, tooth, or claw, or it incorporates images in those shapes.\n\nYou have advantage on saving throws you make to avoid being charmed or frightened or to end those conditions on you."},
  ["creature.slurmy.nrh-tcmc2014"]={title="Slurmy",subtitle="Criatura - NRH-TCMC - 2014",body="Pagina: 10\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCR: 1/8\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 11 (2d8 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 8 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nNimble Escape\n\nSlurmy can take the Disengage or Hide action as a bonus action on each of their turns.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) slashing damage."},
  ["creature.small-drake.psa2014"]={title="Small Drake",subtitle="Criatura - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 33\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["item.small-gold-bracelet.dmg2014"]={title="Small gold bracelet",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.small-gold-idol.dmg2014"]={title="Small gold idol",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.small-gold-statuette-set-with-rubies.dmg2014"]={title="Small gold statuette set with rubies",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 135\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["item.small-mirror-set-in-a-painted-wooden-frame.dmg2014"]={title="Small mirror set in a painted wooden frame",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 134\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["creature.smiler-the-defiler.bgdia2014"]={title="Smiler the Defiler",subtitle="Criatura - BGDIA - 2014",body="Pagina: 133\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: fey / M\n\nCR: 7\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 165 (22d8 + 66)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 20 | CON 16 | INT 18 | WIS 11 | CHA 18\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Common, Elvish, Sylvan\n\nResistencias: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Step {@recharge 4}\n\nAs a bonus action, Smiler can teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space that he can see or to the empty seat of his infernal war machine.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nSmiler has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\nEquipment\n\nSmiler wears +2 leather armor. He carries seven soul coins in a bag and a +1 shortsword\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSmiler makes two weapon attacks. He can cast a spell in place of one of these attacks.\n\n+1 Shortsword\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h9 (1d6 + 6) piercing damage."},
  ["feature.smite-of-protection.xphb2024.paladin.devotion.15"]={title="Smite of Protection",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 114\n\nYour magical smite now radiates protective energy. Whenever you cast XPHB, you and your allies have XPHB while in your Aura of Protection. The aura has this benefit until the start of your next turn."},
  ["item.smith-s-tools.phb2014"]={title="Smith's Tools",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 154\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSmith's tools allow you to work metal, heating it to alter its shape, repair damage, or work raw ingots into useful items.\n\nComponents\n\nSmith's tools include hammers, tongs, charcoal, rags, and a whetstone.\n\nArcana and History\n\nYour expertise lends you additional insight when examining metal objects, such as weapons.\n\nInvestigation\n\nYou can spot clues and make deductions that others might overlook when an investigation involves armor, weapons, or other metalwork.\n\nRepair\n\nWith access to your tools and an open flame hot enough to make metal pliable, you can restore 10 hit points to a damaged metal object for each hour of work.\n\nActivity | DC\n\nSharpen a dull blade | 10\n\nRepair a suit of armor | 15\n\nSunder a nonmagical metal object | 15"},
  ["item.smith-s-tools.xphb2024"]={title="Smith's Tools",subtitle="Item - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 221\n\nRaridade: none\n\n• Ability: Strength\n\n• Utilize: Pry open a door or container (20)\n\n• Craft: Any Melee weapon (except XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB), Medium armor (except XPHB), Heavy armor, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, XPHB"},
  ["item.smoke-grenade.dmg2014"]={title="Smoke Grenade",subtitle="Item - DMG - 2014",body="Pagina: 268\n\nRaridade: none\n\n{#itemEntry Grenade|DMG\n\nOne round after a smoke grenade lands, it emits a cloud of smoke that creates a heavily obscured area in a 20-foot radius. A moderate wind (at least 10 miles per hour) disperses the smoke in 4 rounds; a strong wind (20 or more miles per hour) disperses it in 1 round."},
  ["item.smoke-grenade.xdmg2024"]={title="Smoke Grenade",subtitle="Item - XDMG - 2024",body="Pagina: 73\n\nRaridade: none\n\n{#itemEntry Grenade|XDMG\n\nThe area of the XPHB is XPHB by smoke for 1 minute. A strong wind (such as the XPHB spell) disperses the smoke."},
  ["creature.smoke-mephit.mm2014"]={title="Smoke Mephit",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 217\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 22 (5d6 + 5)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Auran, Ignan\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nWhen the mephit dies, it leaves behind a cloud of smoke that fills a 5-foot-radius sphere centered on its space. The sphere is Vision and Light. Wind disperses the cloud, which otherwise lasts for 1 minute.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting (1/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaws\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h4 (1d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nCinder Breath {@recharge}\n\nThe mephit exhales a 15-foot cone of smoldering ash. Each creature in that area must succeed on a 10 Dexterity saving throw or be blinded until the end of the mephit's next turn."},
  ["creature.smoke-mephit.xmm2024"]={title="Smoke Mephit",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 208\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: elemental / S\n\nCR: 1/4\n\nCA: 12\n\nPV: 13 (3d6 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, fly: 30\n\nSTR 6 | DEX 14 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 10 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Darkvision 60 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Primordial (Auran, Ignan)\n\nImunidades: fire, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: exhaustion, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDeath Burst\n\nThe mephit explodes when it dies. con 11, each creature in a 5-foot XPHB originating from the mephit. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nClaw\n\nm 4, reach 5 ft. h4 (1d4 + 2) Slashing damage.\n\nCinder Breath {@recharge}\n\ndex 11, one creature the mephit can see within 15 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition until the end of the mephit's next turn."},
  ["magicitem.smokepowder.wdh2014"]={title="Smokepowder",subtitle="Item Magico - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 192\n\nRaridade: uncommon\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 400 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 200 PO / 10 dias\n\nSmokepowder is a magical explosive chiefly used to propel a bullet out of the barrel of a firearm. It is stored in airtight wooden kegs or tiny, waterproof leather packets. A packet contains enough smokepowder for five shots, and a keg holds enough smokepowder for five hundred shots.\n\nIf smokepowder is set on fire, dropped, or otherwise handled roughly, it explodes and deals fire damage to each creature or object within 20 feet of it: 1d6 for a packet, 9d6 for a keg. A successful 12 Dexterity saving throw halves the damage.\n\nCasting dispel magic on smokepowder renders it permanently inert."},
  ["background.smuggler.gos2014"]={title="Smuggler",subtitle="Background - GoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 34\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Down Low\n\nYou are acquainted with a network of smugglers who are willing to help you out of tight situations. While in a particular town, city, or other similarly sized community (DM's discretion), you and your companions can stay for free in safe houses. Safe houses provide a poor lifestyle. While staying at a safe house, you can choose to keep your presence (and that of your companions) a secret.\n\nClaim to Fame\n\nEvery smuggler has that one tale that sets them apart from common criminals. By wits, sailing skill, or a silver tongue, you lived to tell the story—and you tell it often. You can roll on the following table to determine your claim or choose one that best fits your character.\n\nd6 | Accomplishment\n\n1 | Spirit of the Whale. You smuggled stolen dwarven spirits in the body of a dead whale being pulled behind a fishing boat. When you delivered the goods, the corpse suddenly exploded, sending whale meat and whiskey bottles for half a mile.\n\n2 | Cart and Sword. You drove a cart filled with stolen art through the middle of a battlefield while singing sea shanties to confuse the combatants.\n\n3 | The Recruit. You enlisted in another nation's navy for the purpose of smuggling stolen jewels to a distant port. You attained a minor rank before disappearing from the navy and making your way here.\n\n4 | River of Shadows. Your riverboat accidentally slipped through the veil into the Shadowfell for several hours. While you were there, you sold some stolen dragonborn artifacts before returning to this plane and paddling home.\n\n5 | Gold-Hearted. You agreed to transport a family escaping a war. The baby began to cry at a checkpoint, and you gave the guards all your gold to let you pass. The family never found out about this gesture.\n\n6 | Playing Both Sides. You once smuggled crates of crossbow bolts and bundles of arrows, each destined for an opposing side in a regional war, at the same time. The buyers arrived within moments of each other but did not discover your trickery.\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nIn general, smugglers value survival, and then profit, above other things. One could be a part of a larger organization, or might run a small smuggling vessel of their own. Smugglers live the lies they have told, and they have a natural ability to recall all the falsehoods and half-truths they have ever spouted.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I love being on the water but hate fishing.\n\n2 | I think of everything in terms of monetary value.\n\n3 | I never stop smiling.\n\n4 | Nothing rattles me; I have a lie for every occasion.\n\n5 | I love gold but won't cheat a friend.\n\n6 | I enjoy doing things others believe to be impossible.\n\n7 | I become wistful when I see the sun rise over the ocean.\n\n8 | I am no common criminal; I am a mastermind.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Wealth Heaps of coins in a secure vault is all I dream of. (Any)\n\n2 | Smuggler's Code I uphold the unwritten rules of the smugglers, who do not cheat one another or directly harm innocents. (Lawful)\n\n3 | All for a Coin I'll do nearly anything if it means I turn a profit. (Evil)\n\n4 | Peace and Prosperity I smuggle only to achieve a greater goal that benefits my community. (Good)\n\n5 | People For all my many lies, I place a high value on friendship. (Any)\n\n6 | Daring I am most happy when risking everything. (Any)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | My vessel was stolen from me, and I burn with the desire to recover it.\n\n2 | I intend to become the leader of the network of smugglers that I belong to.\n\n3 | I owe a debt that cannot be repaid in gold.\n\n4 | After one last job, I will retire from the business.\n\n5 | I was tricked by a fellow smuggler who stole something precious from me. I will find that thief.\n\n6 | I give most of my profits to a charitable cause, and I don't like to brag about it.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | Lying is reflexive, and I sometimes engage in it without realizing.\n\n2 | I tend to assess my relationships in terms of profit and loss.\n\n3 | I believe everyone has a price and am cynical toward those who present themselves as virtuous.\n\n4 | I struggle to trust the words of others.\n\n5 | Few people know the real me.\n\n6 | Though I act charming, I feel nothing for others and don't know what friendship is."},
  ["creature.snake-horror.rot2014"]={title="Snake Horror",subtitle="Criatura - RoT - 2014",body="Pagina: 46\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.snapping-hydra.mcv4ec2014"]={title="Snapping Hydra",subtitle="Criatura - MCV4EC - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: monstrosity / H\n\nCR: 11\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 149 (13d12 + 65)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30, swim: 40\n\nSTR 21 | DEX 5 | CON 21 | INT 2 | WIS 16 | CHA 7\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 60 ft.\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, deafened, frightened, stunned, unconscious\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAmphibious\n\nThe hydra can breathe air and water.\n\nMultiple Heads\n\nThe hydra has five heads. Whenever the hydra takes 30 or more damage in a single turn, one of its heads dies. If all its heads die, the hydra dies.\n\nAt the end of its turn, the hydra grows two heads for each of its heads that died since its last turn, unless it has taken cold damage since its last turn. The hydra regains 10 hit points for each head regrown this way.\n\nReactive Heads\n\nFor each head the hydra has beyond one, it gets an extra reaction that can be used only for opportunity attacks.\n\nWakeful\n\nWhile the hydra sleeps, at least one of its heads is awake.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe hydra makes as many Bite attacks as it has heads.\n\nBite\n\nmw 9 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h14 (2d8 + 5) piercing damage.\n\nShell Defense\n\nThe hydra withdraws its limbs and heads into its shell. Until it emerges as a bonus action, it gains a +4 bonus to AC and has advantage on Strength and Constitution saving throws. While in its shell, the hydra has the prone condition, its speed is 0 and can't increase, its heads can't die, it has disadvantage on Dexterity saving throws, and it can't take any other actions or reactions."},
  ["spell.snare.xge2024"]={title="Snare",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 1 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 165\n\nAs you cast this spell, you use the rope to create a circle with a 5-foot radius on the ground or the floor. When you finish casting, the rope disappears and the circle becomes a magic trap.\n\nThis trap is nearly invisible, requiring a successful Intelligence (Investigation) check against your spell save DC to be discerned.\n\nThe trap triggers when a Small, Medium, or Large creature moves onto the ground or the floor in the spell's radius. That creature must succeed on a Dexterity saving throw or be magically hoisted into the air, leaving it hanging upside down 3 feet above the ground or the floor. The creature is restrained there until the spell ends.\n\nA restrained creature can make a Dexterity saving throw at the end of each of its turns, ending the effect on itself on a success. Alternatively, the creature or someone else who can reach it can use an action to make an Intelligence (Arcana) check against your spell save DC. On a success, the restrained effect ends.\n\nAfter the trap is triggered, the spell ends when no creature is restrained by it."},
  ["creature.snarla.tftyp2014"]={title="Snarla",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 102\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 5\n\nCA: 11/12\n\nPV: 58 (9d8 + 18)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 13 | CON 14 | INT 16 | WIS 11 | CHA 10\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common (can't speak in wolf form)\n\nImunidades: \n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nShapechanger\n\nThe werewolf can use its action to polymorph into a wolf-humanoid hybrid or into a wolf, or back into its true form, which is humanoid. Its statistics, other than its AC, are the same in each form. Any equipment it is wearing or carrying isn't transformed. It reverts to its true form if it dies.\n\nKeen Hearing and Smell\n\nThe werewolf has advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on hearing or smell.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack (Humanoid or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nThe werewolf makes two attacks: one with its bite and one with its claws or spear.\n\nBite (Wolf or Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage. If the target is a humanoid, it must succeed on a 12 Constitution saving throw or be cursed with werewolf MM.\n\nClaws (Hybrid Form Only)\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one creature. h7 (2d4 + 2) slashing damage.\n\nSpear (Humanoid Form Only)\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one creature. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage if used with two hands to make a melee attack."},
  ["creature.sneak.hol2014"]={title="Sneak",subtitle="Criatura - HoL - 2014",body="Pagina: 201\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S\n\nCA: 13\n\nPV: 9 (2d6 + 2)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 13 | CON 12 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 9\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nDagger\n\nmw,rw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 20/60 ft., one target. h3 (1d4 + 1) piercing damage.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nDisengage\n\nYou take the Disengage action."},
  ["feature.sneak-attack.phb2014.rogue.base.1"]={title="Sneak Attack",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 94\n\nBeginning at 1st level, you know how to strike subtly and exploit a foe's distraction. Once per turn, you can deal an extra 1d6 damage to one creature you hit with an attack if you have advantage on the attack roll. The attack must use a finesse or a ranged weapon.\n\nYou don't need advantage on the attack roll if another enemy of the target is within 5 feet of it, that enemy isn't incapacitated, and you don't have disadvantage on the attack roll.\n\nThe amount of the extra damage increases as you gain levels in this class, as shown in the Sneak Attack column of the Rogue table."},
  ["feature.sneak-attack.xphb2024.rogue.base.1"]={title="Sneak Attack",subtitle="Caracteristica - XPHB - 2024",body=""},
  ["magicitem.snicker-snack.wbtw2014"]={title="Snicker-Snack",subtitle="Item Magico - WBtW - 2014",body="Pagina: 213\n\nRaridade: legendary\n\nSintonizacao: Sim\n\nValor padrao 2024: 200000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 100000 PO / 250 dias\n\nYou gain a +3 bonus to attack and damage rolls made with this magic vorpal sword. In addition, the weapon ignores resistance to slashing damage. When you use this weapon to attack a creature that has at least one head and roll a 20 on the attack roll, you cut off one of the creature's heads. The creature dies if it can't survive without the lost head. A creature is immune to this effect if it is immune to slashing damage, it doesn't have or need a head, it has legendary actions, or the DM decides that the creature is too big for its head to be cut off with this weapon. Such a creature instead takes an extra 6d8 slashing damage from the hit.\n\nWhile attuned to Snicker-Snack, you have proficiency with greatswords, and you can use your Charisma modifier instead of your Strength modifier for attack and damage rolls made with the weapon.\n\nSentience\n\nSnicker-Snack is a sentient, chaotic good greatsword with an Intelligence of 9, a Wisdom of 14, and a Charisma of 18. It has hearing and darkvision out to a range of 120 feet. It can speak, read, and understand Common, and its voice sounds silvery and melodic. Snicker-Snack craves the destruction of evil Dragons and urges you to seek out these creatures and slay them.\n\nSnicker-Snack has a fickle personality. It ends its attunement to you if you miss on attack rolls with the weapon three times in a row. Each time you finish a long rest after that happens, you can attempt to regain the sword's trust by making a contested Charisma check against Snicker-Snack. If you win the contest, your attunement to the weapon is instantly restored. Your attunement to the weapon can't be restored in any other way."},
  ["spell.snilloc-s-snowball-swarm.xge2024"]={title="Snilloc's Snowball Swarm",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 2 - XGE - 2024",body="Pagina: 165\n\nA flurry of magic snowballs erupts from a point you choose within range. Each creature in a 5-foot-radius sphere centered on that point must make a Dexterity saving throw. A creature takes 3d6 cold damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.snow-golem.idrotf2014"]={title="Snow Golem",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 308\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: construct / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 8\n\nPV: 39 (6d8 + 12)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 10\n\nSTR 15 | DEX 6 | CON 14 | INT 1 | WIS 6 | CHA 1\n\nSentidos: blindsight 60 ft. (blind beyond this radius)\n\nImunidades: cold, poison\n\nVulnerabilidades: fire\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, paralyzed, petrified, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nCold Absorption\n\nWhenever the golem is subjected to cold damage, it takes no damage and instead regains a number of hit points equal to the cold damage dealt.\n\nImmutable Form\n\nThe golem is immune to any spell or effect that would alter its form.\n\nMelt\n\nWhile in an area of extreme heat, the golem loses 1d6 hit points at the start of each of its turns.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe golem doesn't require air, food, drink, or sleep.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe golem makes three melee attacks.\n\nSlam\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) bludgeoning damage plus 7 (2d6) cold damage.\n\nSnowball\n\nrw 0 to hit, range 60 ft., one target. h9 (2d6 + 2) cold damage."},
  ["creature.snow-leopard.tftyp2014"]={title="Snow Leopard",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 183\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ==="},
  ["creature.snow-maiden.cos2014"]={title="Snow Maiden",subtitle="Criatura - CoS - 2014",body="Pagina: 159\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nImunidades: cold, necrotic, poison"},
  ["item.snowshoes.idrotf2014"]={title="Snowshoes",subtitle="Item - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 20\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSnowshoes reduce the likelihood of their wearer getting stuck in the deep snow."},
  ["creature.snowy-owlbear.idrotf2014"]={title="Snowy Owlbear",subtitle="Criatura - IDRotF - 2014",body="Pagina: 309\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 40, swim: 30"},
  ["creature.snurrevin.tftyp2014"]={title="Snurrevin",subtitle="Criatura - TftYP - 2014",body="Pagina: 53\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 2\n\nCA: 16\n\nPV: 45 (7d8 + 14)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 25\n\nSTR 14 | DEX 11 | CON 14 | INT 14 | WIS 10 | CHA 9\n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Dwarvish, Undercommon\n\nResistencias: poison\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDuergar Resilience\n\nThe duergar has advantage on saving throws against poison, spells, and illusions, as well as to resist being charmed or paralyzed.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, the duergar has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nEnlarge (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nFor 1 minute, the duergar magically increases in size, along with anything it is wearing or carrying. While enlarged, the duergar is Large, doubles its damage dice on Strength-based weapon attacks (included in the attacks), and makes Strength checks and Strength saving throws with advantage. If the duergar lacks the room to become Large, it attains the maximum size possible in the space available.\n\nWar Pick\n\nmw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) piercing damage, or 11 (2d8 + 2) piercing damage while enlarged.\n\nJavelin\n\nmw,rw 4 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 30/120 ft., one target. h5 (1d6 + 2) piercing damage, or 9 (2d6 + 2) piercing damage while enlarged.\n\nInvisibility (Recharges after a Short or Long Rest)\n\nThe duergar magically turns invisible until it attacks, casts a spell, or uses its Enlarge, or until its concentration is broken, up to 1 hour (as if concentration on a spell). Any equipment the duergar wears or carries is invisible with it."},
  ["item.soap.phb2014"]={title="Soap",subtitle="Item - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 150\n\nRaridade: none"},
  ["deity.sobek.phb2014"]={title="Sobek",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 299"},
  ["creature.society-of-sensation-muse.mpp2014"]={title="Society of Sensation Muse",subtitle="Criatura - MPP - 2014",body="Pagina: 61\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / S/M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 44 (8d8 + 8)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 8 | DEX 16 | CON 12 | INT 15 | WIS 14 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus two more languages\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe muse makes two Beguiling Resonance attacks.\n\nBeguiling Resonance\n\nms,rs 5 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 90 ft., one target. h9 (2d8) psychic damage. If the target is a creature, it must succeed on a 13 Charisma saving throw or have disadvantage on the next attack roll it makes until the end of its next turn.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nEnchanting Presence\n\nEach creature within 30 feet of the muse must make a 13 Wisdom saving throw. On a failed save, the creature has the charmed condition for 1 minute. On a successful save, the creature becomes immune to any muse's Enchanting Presence for 24 hours.\n\nWhenever the muse deals damage to the charmed creature, the charmed creature can repeat the saving throw, ending the effect on itself on a success."},
  ["creature.sofina.hat-tg2014"]={title="Sofina",subtitle="Criatura - HAT-TG - 2014",body="=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 15\n\nCA: 14\n\nPV: 161 (19d8 + 76)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 12 | DEX 14 | CON 18 | INT 20 | WIS 14 | CHA 8\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Abyssal, Common, Draconic, Infernal, Thayan\n\nResistencias: necrotic\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nSpecial Equipment\n\nSofina wears a magic robe that grants her a +2 bonus to AC and a +1 bonus to saving throws (included above).\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSofina makes three Necrotic Strike attacks.\n\nNecrotic Strike\n\nms,rs 10 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h32 (5d10 + 5) necrotic damage.\n\nSwarm of Meteors (1/Day)\n\nSofina magically calls down a meteor swarm that detonates in four 40-foot-radius spheres, each one centered on a point she can see within 1 mile of herself. These spheres can overlap. Each creature in one or more of these spheres must make a 18 Dexterity saving throw, taking 35 (10d6) fire damage and 35 (10d6) bludgeoning damage on a failed saving throw, or half as much damage on a successful one. A creature in multiple spheres takes this damage only once.\n\n=== ACOES BONUS ===\n\nSummon Wraith (1/Day)\n\nSofina magically summons the spirit of a Thayan assassin, which appears as a wraith (see the Monster Manual). The summoned wraith appears in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of Sofina, whom it obeys. The summoned wraith takes its turn immediately after Sofina. It lasts for 1 hour, until it or Sofina dies, or until Sofina dismisses it as a bonus action."},
  ["language.solamnic.dsotdq2014"]={title="Solamnic",subtitle="Idioma - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 9"},
  ["creature.solar.mm2014"]={title="Solar",subtitle="Criatura - MM - 2014",body="Pagina: 18\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 243 (18d10 + 144)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, fly: 150\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 22 | CON 26 | INT 25 | WIS 25 | CHA 30\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all, telepathy 120 ft.\n\nResistencias: radiant\n\nImunidades: necrotic, poison\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAngelic Weapons\n\nThe solar's weapon attacks are magical. When the solar hits with any weapon, the weapon deals an extra 6d8 radiant damage (included in the attack).\n\nDivine Awareness\n\nThe solar knows if it hears a lie.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe solar has advantage on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe solar makes two greatsword attacks.\n\nGreatsword\n\nmw 15 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h22 (4d6 + 8) slashing damage plus 27 (6d8) radiant damage.\n\nSlaying Longbow\n\nrw 13 to hit, range 150/600 ft., one target. h15 (2d8 + 6) piercing damage plus 27 (6d8) radiant damage. If the target is a creature that has 100 hit points or fewer, it must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or die.\n\nFlying Sword\n\nThe solar releases its greatsword to hover magically in an unoccupied space within 5 feet of it. If the solar can see the sword, the solar can mentally command it as a bonus action to fly up to 50 feet and either make one attack against a target or return to the solar's hands. If the hovering sword is targeted by any effect, the solar is considered to be holding it. The hovering sword falls if the solar dies.\n\nHealing Touch (4/Day)\n\nThe solar touches another creature. The target magically regains 40 (8d8 + 4) hit points and is freed from any curse, disease, poison, blindness, or deafness.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nTeleport\n\nThe solar magically teleports, along with any equipment it is wearing or carrying, up to 120 feet to an unoccupied space it can see.\n\nSearing Burst (Costs 2 Actions)\n\nThe solar emits magical, divine energy. Each creature of its choice in a 10-foot radius must make a 23 Dexterity saving throw, taking 14 (4d6) fire damage plus 14 (4d6) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one.\n\nBlinding Gaze (Costs 3 Actions)\n\nThe solar targets one creature it can see within 30 feet of it. If the target can see it, the target must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or be blinded until magic such as the lesser restoration spell removes the blindness."},
  ["creature.solar.xmm2024"]={title="Solar",subtitle="Criatura - XMM - 2024",body="Pagina: 288\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: celestial / L\n\nCR: 21\n\nCA: 21\n\nPV: 297 (22d10 + 176)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 50, fly: 150\n\nSTR 26 | DEX 22 | CON 26 | INT 25 | WIS 25 | CHA 30\n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: Truesight 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: all; telepathy 120 ft.\n\nImunidades: poison, radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: charmed, exhaustion, frightened, poisoned\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nDivine Awareness\n\nThe solar knows if it hears a lie.\n\nExalted Restoration\n\nIf the solar dies outside Mount Celestia, its body disappears, and it gains a new body instantly, reviving with all its XPHB somewhere in Mount Celestia.\n\nLegendary Resistance (4/Day)\n\nIf the solar fails a saving throw, it can choose to succeed instead.\n\nMagic Resistance\n\nThe solar has XPHB on saving throws against spells and other magical effects.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\nDivine Aid (3/Day)\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe solar makes two Flying Sword attacks. It can replace one attack with a use of Slaying Bow.\n\nFlying Sword\n\nm,r 15, reach 10 ft. or range 120 ft. h22 (4d6 + 8) Slashing damage plus 36 (8d8) Radiant damage. homThe sword magically returns to the solar's hand or hovers within 5 feet of the solar immediately after a ranged attack.\n\nSlaying Bow\n\ndex 21, one creature the solar can see within 600 feet. actSaveFail If the creature has 100 XPHB or fewer, it dies. It otherwise takes 24 (4d8 + 6) Piercing damage plus 36 (8d8) Radiant damage.\n\n=== ACOES LENDARIAS ===\n\nBlinding Gaze\n\ncon 25, one creature the solar can see within 120 feet. actSaveFail The target has the XPHB condition for 1 minute. actSaveSuccessOrFail The solar can't take this action again until the start of its next turn.\n\nRadiant Teleport\n\nThe solar teleports up to 60 feet to an unoccupied space it can see. dex 25, each creature in a 10-foot XPHB originating from the solar at its destination space. actSaveFail 11 (2d10) Radiant damage. actSaveSuccess Half damage."},
  ["creature.solar-bastion-knight.bmt2014"]={title="Solar Bastion Knight",subtitle="Criatura - BMT - 2014",body="Pagina: 75\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 9\n\nCA: 20\n\nPV: 150 (20d8 + 60)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 18 | DEX 10 | CON 17 | INT 15 | WIS 16 | CHA 17\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: Common plus any one language\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded, charmed, frightened\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nAura of Protection\n\nThe knight and each ally within 10 feet of it have advantage on saving throws. This trait is suppressed while the knight has the incapacitated condition.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nSpellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe knight makes three Sunspear attacks.\n\nSunspear\n\nms,rs 8 to hit, reach 5 ft. or range 120 ft., one target. h14 (3d6 + 4) radiant damage, or 21 (5d6 + 4) radiant damage if the target is a Fiend or an Undead.\n\nSolar Flare {@recharge 5}\n\nThe knight unleashes a blaze of brilliant energy that fills a 30-foot-radius sphere centered on the knight. Each creature of the knight's choice in that area must make a 15 Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 22 (4d10) radiant damage and has the blinded condition until the end of its next turn. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only. For the next minute, the affected area is filled with bright light that is sunlight."},
  ["creature.solar-dragon-wyrmling.bam2014"]={title="Solar Dragon Wyrmling",subtitle="Criatura - BAM - 2014",body="Pagina: 53\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: dragon / M\n\nCR: 3\n\nCA: 15\n\nPV: 51 (6d8 + 24)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 20, fly: 40\n\nSTR 16 | DEX 15 | CON 18 | INT 11 | WIS 12 | CHA 10\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Draconic\n\nImunidades: radiant\n\nImunidades a condicoes: blinded\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFlyby\n\nThe dragon doesn't provoke opportunity attacks when it flies out of an enemy's reach.\n\nUnusual Nature\n\nThe dragon doesn't require air.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe dragon makes one Bite attack and one Tail attack.\n\nBite\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d6 + 3) piercing damage plus 3 (1d6) radiant damage.\n\nTail\n\nmw 5 to hit, reach 10 ft., one target. h5 (1d4 + 3) bludgeoning damage.\n\nPhotonic Breath {@recharge 5}\n\nThe dragon exhales a flashing mote of radiant energy that travels to a point the dragon can see within 120 feet of itself, then blossoms into a 10-foot-radius sphere centered on that point. Each creature in the sphere must make a 14 Constitution saving throw, taking 22 (4d10) radiant damage on a failed save, or half as much damage on a successful one."},
  ["creature.soldier.ggr2014"]={title="Soldier",subtitle="Criatura - GGR - 2014",body="Pagina: 226\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 1/2\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 16 (3d8 + 3)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 12 | CON 12 | INT 10 | WIS 11 | CHA 11\n\nPericias: \n\nIdiomas: any one language (usually Common)\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFormation Tactics\n\nThe soldier has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, frightened, grappled, or restrained while it is within 5 feet of at least one ally.\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nThe soldier makes two melee attacks.\n\nLongsword\n\nmw 3 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h6 (1d8 + 2) slashing damage, or 7 (1d10 + 2) slashing damage if used with two hands."},
  ["background.soldier.phb2014"]={title="Soldier",subtitle="Background - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 140\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiencies:\n\n• Equipment:\n\nFeature: Military Rank\n\nYou have a military rank from your career as a soldier. Soldiers loyal to your former military organization still recognize your authority and influence, and they defer to you if they are of a lower rank. You can invoke your rank to exert influence over other soldiers and requisition simple equipment or horses for temporary use. You can also usually gain access to friendly military encampments and fortresses where your rank is recognized.\n\nSpecialty\n\nDuring your time as a soldier, you had a specific role to play in your unit or army. Roll a d8 or choose from the options in the table below to determine your role:\n\nd8 | Role\n\n1 | Officer\n\n2 | Scout\n\n3 | Infantry\n\n4 | Cavalry\n\n5 | Healer\n\n6 | Quartermaster\n\n7 | Standard-bearer\n\n8 | Support staff (cook, blacksmith, or the like)\n\nSuggested Characteristics\n\nThe horrors of war combined with the rigid discipline of military service leave their mark on all soldiers, shaping their ideals, creating strong bonds, and often leaving them scarred and vulnerable to fear, shame, and hatred.\n\nd8 | Personality Trait\n\n1 | I'm always polite and respectful.\n\n2 | I'm haunted by memories of war. I can't get the images of violence out of my mind.\n\n3 | I've lost too many friends, and I'm slow to make new ones.\n\n4 | I'm full of inspiring and cautionary tales from my military experience relevant to almost every combat situation.\n\n5 | I can stare down a hell hound without flinching.\n\n6 | I enjoy being strong and like breaking things.\n\n7 | I have a crude sense of humor.\n\n8 | I face problems head-on. A simple, direct solution is the best path to success.\n\nd6 | Ideal\n\n1 | Greater Good. Our lot is to lay down our lives in defense of others. (Good)\n\n2 | Responsibility. I do what I must and obey just authority. (Lawful)\n\n3 | Independence. When people follow orders blindly, they embrace a kind of tyranny. (Chaotic)\n\n4 | Might. In life as in war, the stronger force wins. (Evil)\n\n5 | Live and Let Live. Ideals aren't worth killing over or going to war for. (Neutral)\n\n6 | Nation. My city, nation, or people are all that matter. (Any)\n\nd6 | Bond\n\n1 | I would still lay down my life for the people I served with.\n\n2 | Someone saved my life on the battlefield. To this day, I will never leave a friend behind.\n\n3 | My honor is my life.\n\n4 | I'll never forget the crushing defeat my company suffered or the enemies who dealt it.\n\n5 | Those who fight beside me are those worth dying for.\n\n6 | I fight for those who cannot fight for themselves.\n\nd6 | Flaw\n\n1 | The monstrous enemy we faced in battle still leaves me quivering with fear.\n\n2 | I have little respect for anyone who is not a proven warrior.\n\n3 | I made a terrible mistake in battle that cost many lives—and I would do anything to keep that mistake secret.\n\n4 | My hatred of my enemies is blinding and unreasoning.\n\n5 | I obey the law, even if the law causes misery.\n\n6 | I'd rather eat my armor than admit when I'm wrong."},
  ["background.soldier.xphb2024"]={title="Soldier",subtitle="Background - XPHB - 2024",body="Pagina: 185\n\n• Ability Scores:\n\n• Feat:\n\n• Skill Proficiencies:\n\n• Tool Proficiency:\n\n• Equipment:"},
  ["subclass.solidarity-domain-psa.psa2014.cleric.solidarity-psa.0"]={title="Solidarity Domain (PSA)",subtitle="Subclasse - PSA - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA SUBCLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Bonus Proficiency\n\nPagina: 24\n\nWhen you choose this domain at 1st level, you gain proficiency with heavy armor.\n\nNivel 1 - Solidarity Domain (PSA)\n\nPagina: 24\n\nThe worthy must know and respect all others whom the God-Pharaoh deems worthy, for in the afterlife, all will be united in purpose and action.\n\nOketra is charged with expounding upon this teaching of the God-Pharaoh, instilling in every initiate the virtue of solidarity. She forges each group of children into a crop of acolytes with just one purpose: to be judged worthy of a glorious afterlife. And she instills in each crop the ability to unite in a single action in pursuit of that purpose. She is fond of poetic imagery to communicate her ideals.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | bless, guiding bolt\n\n3rd | aid, warding bond\n\n5th | beacon of hope, crusader's mantle\n\n7th | aura of life, guardian of faith\n\n9th | circle of power, mass cure wounds\n\nNivel 1 - Solidarity's Action\n\nPagina: 24\n\nAlso at 1st level, when you take the Help action to aid an ally's attack, you can make one weapon attack as a bonus action. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain expended uses when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 2 - Channel Divinity: Preserve Life\n\nPagina: 24\n\nStarting at 2nd level, you can use your Channel Divinity to heal the badly injured.\n\nAs an action, you present your holy symbol and evoke healing energy that can restore a number of hit points equal to five times your cleric level. Choose any creatures within 30 feet of you, and divide those hit points among them. This feature can restore a creature to no more than half of its hit point maximum. You can't use this feature on an undead or a construct.\n\nNivel 3 - Channel Divinity: Preserve Life\n\nNivel 3 - Solidarity Domain (PSA)\n\nNivel 6 - Oketra's Blessing\n\nPagina: 24\n\nAt 6th level, when a creature within 30 feet of you makes an attack roll, you can use your reaction to grant that creature a +10 bonus to the roll, using your Channel Divinity. You make this choice after you see the roll, but before the DM says whether the attack hits or misses.\n\nNivel 8 - Blessed Strikes\n\nPagina: 30\n\n{@i 8th-level cleric tce, which replaces the Divine Strike feature\n\nYou are blessed with divine might in battle. When a creature takes damage from one of your cantrips or weapon attacks, you can also deal 1d8 radiant damage to that creature. Once you deal this damage, you can't use this feature again until the start of your next turn.\n\nNivel 8 - Divine Strike\n\nPagina: 24\n\nAt 8th level, you gain the ability to infuse your weapon strikes with divine energy. Once on each of your turns when you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can cause the attack to deal an extra 1d8 damage of the same type dealt by the weapon to the target. When you reach 14th level, the extra damage increases to 2d8.\n\nNivel 17 - Supreme Healing\n\nPagina: 24\n\nStarting at 17th level, when you would normally roll one or more dice to restore hit points with a spell, you instead use the highest number possible for each die. For example, instead of restoring 2d6 hit points to a creature, you restore 12."},
  ["feature.solidarity-domain-psa.psa2014.cleric.solidarity-psa.1"]={title="Solidarity Domain (PSA)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nThe worthy must know and respect all others whom the God-Pharaoh deems worthy, for in the afterlife, all will be united in purpose and action.\n\nOketra is charged with expounding upon this teaching of the God-Pharaoh, instilling in every initiate the virtue of solidarity. She forges each group of children into a crop of acolytes with just one purpose: to be judged worthy of a glorious afterlife. And she instills in each crop the ability to unite in a single action in pursuit of that purpose. She is fond of poetic imagery to communicate her ideals.\n\nAt each indicated cleric level, add the listed spells to your spells prepared.\n\nCleric Level | Spells\n\n1st | bless, guiding bolt\n\n3rd | aid, warding bond\n\n5th | beacon of hope, crusader's mantle\n\n7th | aura of life, guardian of faith\n\n9th | circle of power, mass cure wounds"},
  ["feature.solidarity-domain-psa.psa2014.cleric.solidarity-psa.3"]={title="Solidarity Domain (PSA)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body=""},
  ["feature.solidarity-s-action.psa2014.cleric.solidarity-psa.1"]={title="Solidarity's Action",subtitle="Caracteristica - PSA - 2014",body="Pagina: 24\n\nAlso at 1st level, when you take the Help action to aid an ally's attack, you can make one weapon attack as a bonus action. You can use this feature a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). You regain expended uses when you finish a long rest."},
  ["deity.solinari.dsotdq2014"]={title="Solinari",subtitle="Divindade - DSotDQ - 2014",body="Pagina: 15\n\nSolinari, the god of good magic, is patron of the Mages of High Sorcery's Order of the White Robes and other benevolent mages. His power manifests through the white moon of Krynn, the brightest of its three moons. Along with his cousins Lunitari and Nuitari, he watches Krynn from the heavens and encourages magic that aids, heals, and protects."},
  ["deity.solinari.phb2014"]={title="Solinari",subtitle="Divindade - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 295"},
  ["deity.solonor-thelandira.mtf2014"]={title="Solonor Thelandira",subtitle="Divindade - MTF - 2014",body="Pagina: 43"},
  ["deity.solonor-thelandira.scag2014"]={title="Solonor Thelandira",subtitle="Divindade - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 23"},
  ["creature.soluun-xibrindas.wdh2014"]={title="Soluun Xibrindas",subtitle="Criatura - WDH - 2014",body="Pagina: 202\n\n=== ESTATISTICAS ===\n\nTipo/Tamanho: humanoid / M\n\nCR: 4\n\nCA: 18\n\nPV: 84 (13d8 + 26)\n\nDeslocamento: walk: 30\n\nSTR 13 | DEX 18 | CON 14 | INT 11 | WIS 13 | CHA 14\n\nSalvamentos: \n\nPericias: \n\nSentidos: darkvision 120 ft.\n\nIdiomas: Elvish, Undercommon\n\n=== TRACOS ===\n\nFey Ancestry\n\nSoluun has advantage on saving throws against being charmed, and magic can't put Soluun to sleep.\n\nGunslinger\n\nBeing within 5 feet of a hostile creature or attacking at long range doesn't impose disadvantage on Soluun's ranged attack rolls with a pistol. In addition, Soluun ignores Cover and Cover when making ranged attacks with a pistol.\n\nSunlight Sensitivity\n\nWhile in sunlight, Soluun has disadvantage on attack rolls, as well as on Wisdom (Perception) checks that rely on sight.\n\nEquipment\n\nFour packets of smokepowder and a pouch containing 20 pistol bullets\n\nBoots of Elvenkind\n\nWhilst wearing these boots Soluun's steps make no sound and he has advantage on any Dexterity (Stealth) checks that rely on moving silently.\n\n=== CONJURACAO ===\n\nInnate Spellcasting\n\n=== ACOES ===\n\nMultiattack\n\nSoluun makes two scimitar attacks.\n\nScimitar\n\nmw 6 to hit, reach 5 ft., one target. h7 (1d6 + 4) slashing damage.\n\nPoisonous Pistol\n\nrw 6 to hit, range 30/90 ft., one target. h9 (1d10 + 4) piercing damage plus 11 (2d10) poison damage."},
  ["magicitem.somniferous-blossom-rod.au2014"]={title="Somniferous Blossom Rod",subtitle="Item Magico - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 127\n\nRaridade: very rare\n\nSintonizacao: Nao\n\nValor padrao 2024: 40000 PO\n\nCrafting 2024: 20000 PO / 125 dias"},
  ["feature.song-of-defense.frhof2014.wizard.bladesinger.10"]={title="Song of Defense",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nWhen you take damage while your Bladesong is active, you can take a XPHB to expend one spell slot and reduce the damage taken by an amount equal to five times the spell slot's level."},
  ["feature.song-of-defense.tce2014.wizard.bladesinging.10"]={title="Song of Defense",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nBeginning at 10th level, you can direct your magic to absorb damage while your bladesong is active. When you take damage, you can use your reaction to expend one spell slot and reduce that damage to you by an amount equal to five times the spell's slot level."},
  ["feature.song-of-rest-d10.phb2014.bard.base.13"]={title="Song of Rest (d10)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nAt 13th level, the extra hit points gained from Song of Rest increases to 1d10."},
  ["feature.song-of-rest-d12.phb2014.bard.base.17"]={title="Song of Rest (d12)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nAt 17th level, the extra hit points gained from Song of Rest increases to 1d12."},
  ["feature.song-of-rest-d6.phb2014.bard.base.2"]={title="Song of Rest (d6)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nBeginning at 2nd level, you can use soothing music or oration to help revitalize your wounded allies during a short rest. If you or any friendly creatures who can hear your performance regain hit points by spending Hit Dice at the end of the short rest, each of those creatures regains an extra 1d6 hit points.\n\nThe extra hit points increase when you reach certain levels in this class: to 1d8 at 9th level, to 1d10 at 13th level, and to 1d12 at 17th level."},
  ["feature.song-of-rest-d8.phb2014.bard.base.9"]={title="Song of Rest (d8)",subtitle="Caracteristica - PHB - 2014",body="Pagina: 51\n\nAt 9th level, the extra hit points gained from Song of Rest increases to 1d8."},
  ["feature.song-of-victory.frhof2014.wizard.bladesinger.14"]={title="Song of Victory",subtitle="Caracteristica - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 27\n\nAfter you cast a spell that has a casting time of an action, you can make one attack with a weapon as a XPHB."},
  ["feature.song-of-victory.tce2014.wizard.bladesinging.14"]={title="Song of Victory",subtitle="Caracteristica - TCE - 2014",body="Pagina: 76\n\nStarting at 14th level, you add your Intelligence modifier (minimum of +1) to the damage of your melee weapon attacks while your Bladesong is active."},
  ["spell.songal-s-elemental-suffusion.frhof2014"]={title="Songal's Elemental Suffusion",subtitle="Magia - Nivel 5 - FRHoF - 2014",body="Pagina: 145\n\nYou imbue yourself with the elemental power of genies. You gain the following benefits until the spell ends:\n\n• Elemental Immunity When you cast this spell, choose one of the following damage types: Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. You have XPHB to the chosen damage type.\n\n• Elemental Pulse When you cast this spell and at the start of each of your subsequent turns, you release a burst of elemental energy in a 15-foot XPHB originating from yourself. Each creature of your choice in that area makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failed save, a creature takes 2d6 Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (your choice) and has the XPHB condition. On a successful save, a creature takes half as much damage only.\n\n• Flight You gain a XPHB of 30 feet and can hover.\n\nCasting as a Circle Spell\n\nIf the spell is cast as a Circle spell, its casting time increases to 1 minute, and its duration increases to XPHB, up to 10 minutes. For each secondary caster who participates in the casting, you can choose one additional creature, to a maximum of nine additional creatures. The chosen creatures also gain the benefits of the spell for its duration.\n\nWhen the spell is cast, each secondary caster must expend a level 2+ spell slot; otherwise, the spell fails."},
  ["item.songhorn.scag2014"]={title="Songhorn",subtitle="Item - SCAG - 2014",body="Pagina: 124\n\nRaridade: none\n\nA recorder, a simple type of flute, usually carved from wood."},
  ["feat.soothing-familiar.au2014"]={title="Soothing Familiar",subtitle="Feat - AU - 2014",body="Pagina: 31\n\nYou gain the following benefits.\n\nHealing Beacon\n\nPositive energy fills a 5-foot XPHB originating from your familiar as long as it is within 120 feet of you. Whenever an ally in that XPHB rolls a die to determine the number of XPHB restored to a creature, that ally can treat a roll of 1 or 2 on the die as a 3."},
  ["item.soothsalts.egw2014"]={title="Soothsalts",subtitle="Item - EGW - 2014",body="Pagina: 152\n\nRaridade: none\n\nSoothsalts are derived from a naturally occurring crystalline substance discovered throughout the wilds of the Miskath Strand. The crimson crystals have been mined from cavernous veins like those in the mouth of the Miskath Pit and found within smaller geode formations near sites ravaged by the Calamity. Soothsalts are consumed orally in lozenge-sized doses, and frequent users can be identified by the telltale crimson stain around their mouths. A creature subjected to a dose of soothsalts gains advantage on all Intelligence checks for 1d4 hours.\n\nFor each dose of soothsalts consumed, the creature must succeed on a 15 Constitution saving throw or gain one level of exhaustion—an effect which is cumulative with multiple doses."},
  ["class.sorcerer.phb2014"]={title="Sorcerer",subtitle="Classe - PHB - 2014",body="=== CARACTERISTICAS DA CLASSE ===\n\nNivel 1 - Innate Sorcery\n\nPagina: 140\n\nAn event in your past left an indelible mark on you, infusing you with simmering magic. As a XPHB, you can unleash that magic for 1 minute, during which you gain the following benefits:\n\n• The spell save DC of your Sorcerer spells increases by 1.\n\n• You have XPHB on the attack rolls of Sorcerer spells you cast.\n\nYou can use this feature twice, and you regain all expended uses of it when you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 1 - Innate Sorcery\n\nNivel 1 - Sorcerous Origin\n\nPagina: 99\n\nChoose a sorcerous origin, which describes the source of your innate magical power, from the list of available origins.\n\nYour choice grants you features when you choose it at 1st level and again at 6th, 14th, and 18th level.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAn event in your past, or in the life of a parent or ancestor, left an indelible mark on you, infusing you with arcane magic. This font of magic, whatever its origin, fuels your spells. See PHB for the general rules of spellcasting and PHB for the spells.\n\nCantrips\n\nAt 1st level, you know four cantrips of your choice from the sorcerer spell list. You learn an additional sorcerer cantrip of your choice at 4th level and another at 10th level.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Sorcerer table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your spells of 1st level and higher. To cast one of these sorcerer spells, you must expend a slot of the spell's level or higher. You regain all expended spell slots when you finish a long rest.\n\nFor example, if you know the 1st-level spell burning hands and have a 1st-level and a 2nd-level spell slot available, you can cast burning hands using either slot.\n\nSpells Known of 1st Level and Higher\n\nYou know two 1st-level spells of your choice from the sorcerer spell list.\n\nYou learn an additional sorcerer spell of your choice at each level except 12th, 14th, 16th, 18th, 19th, and 20th. Each of these spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For instance, when you reach 3rd level in this class, you can learn one new spell of 1st or 2nd level.\n\nAdditionally, when you gain a level in this class, you can choose one of the sorcerer spells you know and replace it with another spell from the sorcerer spell list, which also must be of a level for which you have spell slots.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nCharisma is your spellcasting ability for your sorcerer spells, since the power of your magic relies on your ability to project your will into the world. You use your Charisma whenever a spell refers to your spellcasting ability. In addition, you use your Charisma modifier when setting the saving throw DC for a sorcerer spell you cast and when making an attack roll with one.\n\nSpell\n\nSpell\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an phb as a spellcasting focus for your sorcerer spells.\n\nNivel 1 - Spellcasting\n\nPagina: 139\n\nDrawing from your innate magic, you can cast spells. See XPHB for the rules on spellcasting. The information below details how you use those rules with Sorcerer spells, which appear in the spells later in the class's description.\n\nCantrips\n\nYou know four Sorcerer cantrips of your choice. XPHB, XPHB, XPHB, and XPHB are recommended. Whenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one of your cantrips from this feature with another Sorcerer cantrip of your choice.\n\nWhen you reach Sorcerer levels 4 and 10, you learn another Sorcerer cantrip of your choice, as shown in the Cantrips column of the Sorcerer Features table.\n\nSpell Slots\n\nThe Sorcerer Features table shows how many spell slots you have to cast your level 1+ spells. You regain all expended slots when you finish a XPHB.\n\nPrepared Spells of Level 1+\n\nYou prepare the list of level 1+ spells that are available for you to cast with this feature. To start, choose two level 1 Sorcerer spells. XPHB and XPHB are recommended.\n\nThe number of spells on your list increases as you gain Sorcerer levels, as shown in the Prepared Spells column of the Sorcerer Features table. Whenever that number increases, choose additional Sorcerer spells until the number of spells on your list matches the number in the Sorcerer Features table. The chosen spells must be of a level for which you have spell slots. For example, if you're a level 3 Sorcerer, your list of prepared spells can include six Sorcerer spells of level 1 or 2 in any combination.\n\nIf another Sorcerer feature gives you spells that you always have prepared, those spells don't count against the number of spells you can prepare with this feature, but those spells otherwise count as Sorcerer spells for you.\n\nChanging Your Prepared Spells\n\nWhenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one spell on your list with another Sorcerer spell for which you have spell slots.\n\nSpellcasting Ability\n\nCharisma is your spellcasting ability for your Sorcerer spells.\n\nSpellcasting Focus\n\nYou can use an XPHB as a XPHB for your Sorcerer spells.\n\nNivel 2 - Flexible Casting\n\nPagina: 99\n\nYou can use your sorcery points to gain additional spell slots, or sacrifice spell slots to gain additional sorcery points. You learn other ways to use your sorcery points as you reach higher levels.\n\nCreating Spell Slots\n\nYou can transform unexpended sorcery points into one spell slot as a bonus action on your turn. The created spell slots vanish at the end of a long rest. The Creating Spell Slots table shows the cost of creating a spell slot of a given level. You can create spell slots no higher in level than 5th.\n\nSpell Slot Level | Sorcery Point Cost\n\n1st | 2\n\n2nd | 3\n\n3rd | 5\n\n4th | 6\n\n5th | 7\n\nConverting a Spell Slot to Sorcery Points\n\nAs a bonus action on your turn, you can expend one spell slot and gain a number of sorcery points equal to the slot's level.\n\nNivel 2 - Font of Magic\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 2nd level, you tap into a deep wellspring of magic within yourself. This wellspring is represented by sorcery points, which allow you to create a variety of magical effects.\n\nNivel 2 - Font of Magic\n\nPagina: 140\n\nYou can tap into the wellspring of magic within yourself. This wellspring is represented by Sorcery Points, which allow you to create a variety of magical effects.\n\nYou have 2 Sorcery Points, and you gain more as you reach higher levels, as shown in the Sorcery Points column of the Sorcerer Features table. You can't have more Sorcery Points than the number shown in the table for your level. You regain all expended Sorcery Points when you finish a XPHB.\n\nYou can use your Sorcery Points to fuel the options below, along with other features, such as Metamagic, that use those points.\n\nConverting Spell Slots to Sorcery Points\n\nYou can expend a spell slot to gain a number of Sorcery Points equal to the slot's level (no action required).\n\nCreating Spell Slots\n\nAs a XPHB, you can transform unexpended Sorcery Points into one spell slot. The Creating Spell Slots table shows the cost of creating a spell slot of a given level, and it lists the minimum Sorcerer level you must be to create a slot. You can create a spell slot no higher than level 5.\n\nAny spell slot you create with this feature vanishes when you finish a XPHB.\n\nSpell Slot Level | Sorcery Point Cost | Min. Sorcerer Level\n\n1 | 2 | 2\n\n2 | 3 | 3\n\n3 | 5 | 5\n\n4 | 6 | 7\n\n5 | 7 | 9\n\nNivel 2 - Font of Magic\n\nNivel 2 - Font of Magic\n\nNivel 2 - Metamagic\n\nPagina: 141\n\nBecause your magic flows from within, you can alter your spells to suit your needs; you gain two Metamagic options of your choice from \"optionalfeatures\" later in this class's description. You use the chosen options to temporarily modify spells you cast. To use an option, you must spend the number of Sorcery Points that it costs.\n\nYou can use only one Metamagic option on a spell when you cast it unless otherwise noted in one of those options.\n\nWhenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one of your Metamagic options with one you don't know. You gain two more options at Sorcerer level 10 and two more at Sorcerer level 17.\n\nNivel 2 - Metamagic Options\n\nPagina: 141\n\nThe following options are available to your Metamagic feature. The options are presented in alphabetical order.\n\nNivel 2 - Metamagic Options\n\nNivel 2 - Sorcery Points\n\nPagina: 99\n\nYou have 2 sorcery points, and you gain one additional point every time you level up, to a maximum of 20 at level 20. You can never have more sorcery points than shown on the table for your level. You regain all spent sorcery points when you finish a long rest.\n\nNivel 2 - Sorcery Points\n\nNivel 3 - Metamagic\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 3rd level, you gain the ability to twist your spells to suit your needs. You gain two of the following Metamagic options of your choice. You gain another one at 10th and 17th level.\n\nYou can use only one Metamagic option on a spell when you cast it, unless otherwise noted.\n\nNivel 3 - Metamagic\n\nAt 3rd level, you gain the ability to twist your spells to suit your needs. You gain two Metamagic options of your choice. You gain another one at 10th and 17th level.\n\nYou can use only one Metamagic option on a spell when you cast it, unless otherwise noted.\n\nNivel 3 - Metamagic Options\n\nPagina: 65\n\n{@i 3rd-level sorcerer tce\n\nWhen you choose Metamagic options, you have access to the following additional options.\n\nNivel 3 - Metamagic Options\n\nNivel 3 - Sorcerer Subclass\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain a Sorcerer subclass of your choice. A subclass is a specialization that grants you features at certain Sorcerer levels. For the rest of your career, you gain each of your subclass's features that are of your Sorcerer level or lower.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 99\n\nWhen you reach 4th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 4 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. You gain this feature again at Sorcerer levels 8, 12, and 16.\n\nNivel 4 - Sorcerous Versatility\n\nPagina: 65\n\n{@i 4th-level sorcerer tce\n\nWhenever you reach a level in this class that grants the Ability Score Improvement feature, you can do one of the following, representing the magic within you flowing in new ways:\n\n• Replace one of the options you chose for the Metamagic feature with a different optionalfeatures available to you.\n\n• Replace one cantrip you learned from this class's Spellcasting feature with another cantrip from the spells.\n\nNivel 5 - Magical Guidance\n\nPagina: 65\n\n{@i 5th-level sorcerer tce\n\nYou can tap into your inner wellspring of magic to try to conjure success from failure. When you make an ability check that fails, you can spend 1 sorcery point to reroll the d20, and you must use the new roll, potentially turning the failure into a success.\n\nNivel 5 - Sorcerous Restoration\n\nPagina: 141\n\nWhen you finish a XPHB, you can regain expended Sorcery Points, but no more than a number equal to half your Sorcerer level (round down). Once you use this feature, you can't do so again until you finish a XPHB.\n\nNivel 5 - Sorcerous Restoration\n\nNivel 6 - Sorcerous Origin feature\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 6th level, you gain a feature granted by your Sorcerous Origin.\n\nNivel 6 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain a feature from your Sorcerer subclass.\n\nNivel 7 - Sorcery Incarnate\n\nPagina: 141\n\nIf you have no uses of Innate Sorcery left, you can use it if you spend 2 Sorcery Points when you take the XPHB to activate it.\n\nIn addition, while your Innate Sorcery feature is active, you can use up to two of your optionalfeatures on each spell you cast.\n\nNivel 7 - Sorcery Incarnate\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 99\n\nWhen you reach 8th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 8 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 10 - Metamagic\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 10th level, you learn an additional metamagic option.\n\nNivel 10 - Metamagic\n\nPagina: 141\n\nBecause your magic flows from within you, you can alter your spells to suit your needs; you gain two Metamagic options of your choice from the \"optionalfeatures\" section later in this class's description.\n\nYou can use only one Metamagic option on a spell when you cast it, unless otherwise noted in one of those options.\n\nWhenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one of your Metamagic options with one you don't know.\n\nNivel 10 - Metamagic\n\nNivel 10 - Metamagic\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 99\n\nWhen you reach 12th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 12 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 14 - Sorcerous Origin feature\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 14th level, you gain a feature granted by your Sorcerous Origin.\n\nNivel 14 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain a feature from your Sorcerer subclass.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 99\n\nWhen you reach 16th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 16 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain the XPHB feat or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify.\n\nNivel 17 - Metamagic\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 17th level, you learn an additional metamagic option.\n\nNivel 17 - Metamagic\n\nPagina: 141\n\nBecause your magic flows from within you, you can alter your spells to suit your needs; you gain two Metamagic options of your choice from the \"optionalfeatures\" section later in this class's description.\n\nYou can use only one Metamagic option on a spell when you cast it, unless otherwise noted in one of those options.\n\nWhenever you gain a Sorcerer level, you can replace one of your Metamagic options with one you don't know.\n\nNivel 17 - Metamagic\n\nNivel 17 - Metamagic\n\nNivel 18 - Sorcerous Origin feature\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 18th level, you gain a feature granted by your Sorcerous Origin.\n\nNivel 18 - Subclass Feature\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain a feature from your Sorcerer subclass.\n\nNivel 19 - Ability Score Improvement\n\nPagina: 99\n\nWhen you reach 19th level, you can increase one ability score of your choice by 2, or you can increase two ability scores of your choice by 1. As normal, you can't increase an ability score above 20 using this feature.\n\nIf your DM allows the use of feats, you may instead take a feats.html.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nPagina: 141\n\nYou gain an feats or another feats.html of your choice for which you qualify. XPHB is recommended.\n\nNivel 19 - Epic Boon\n\nNivel 20 - Arcane Apotheosis\n\nPagina: 141\n\nWhile your Innate Sorcery feature is active, you can use one Metamagic option on each of your turns without spending Sorcery Points on it.\n\nNivel 20 - Sorcerous Restoration\n\nPagina: 99\n\nAt 20th level, you regain 4 expended sorcery points whenever you finish a short rest."},
